\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr, won down on econ worries,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  caution\b0\par\par\uc2 1,024 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 04:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Sing dlr at two-week low on U.S. dlr short covering\par \par \uc2 * Won turns down on stock outflows\par \par \uc2 * Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may prompt more AXJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -analysts\par \par \uc2 (Updates text, prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar and the South Korean won fell on Thursday as investors reduced positions in emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on increasing concerns over a global economic slowdown and after Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 Japan sold an estimated 1.6 trillion yen in the market and its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased monetary policy, following Switzerland in efforts to tame \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  buoyed by safe-heaven demand from investors fretting about the health of the global economy.\par \par \uc2 "Japan's action does show the concern shared by central banks in the region about the strength of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At the margin, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will encourage other central banks to keep doing what they have been doing," said Frances Cheung, a strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 "In this risk off environment, and especially with this partly coming from worries of a U.S. slowdown, Asia could be impacted negatively. So I getting more cautious towards Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term."\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities have been spotted buying dollars in recent weeks to stem upward pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and maintain export competitiveness amid slackening global growth, although they are fighting inflation at the same time.\par \par \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2 's Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Andy Ji sees more dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, saying Singapore, Taiwan and \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  are more likely to keep curbing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength in Asia.\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have enjoyed continuous inflows despite worries about a global slowdown and debt problems in the United States and Europe as the region has stronger economic and fiscal fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The regional units may enjoy more inflows, especially if the U.S. Federal Reserve conducts further easing while some Asian countries are still trying to contain inflation, many analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, former Fed Vice Chairman Donald Kohn said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might need to give serious consideration to more easing to spur the world's top economy.\par \par \uc2 "Unless the QE3 revives a mechanism of credit creation and increases M1 as much as reserve base, that will just boost inflation not rehabilitate the economy," says Lee Jin-woo, research head of NH Investment & Futures in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 "It's difficult for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other riskier assets to rise, given the situation."\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar hit a two-week low against the greenback on U.S. dollar-short covering.\par \par \uc2 The city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen finding relief from demand from long-term investors, but is expected to remain under pressure in the short-term pressure if global growth worries spur more profit taking.\par \par \uc2 "The market is taking profit. But lots of people are still trying to see where to short dollar/Asia as it's not a fault from Asia but from the U.S. and EU," said a dealer, adding he prefer short U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Still, we can wait. There is no need to hurry to sell now."\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won turned lower on stock outflows and local shares hit their lowest close in more than four months.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have been net sellers of Seoul stocks during the three sessions in a row. They dumped a combined more than $1 billion on Wednesday and Thursday. In the previous session, their stock sales were largest since May.\par \par \uc2 "Stocks look ugly and dollar/won seem to have room to rise, probably to 1,065," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 But some expect the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rebound, saying investors appeared to hold dollar-long positions.\par \par \uc2 The 14-day dollar/won Relative Strength Index (RSI) rose to 51.5, the highest since late June and well above the 30 threshold, indicating the pair is not in oversold territory.\par \par \uc2 Long-term investors still favour the country's assets.\par \par \uc2 "In countries such as Australia or South Korea, we believe investors can access relatively high yield potential without taking what we consider to be too much duration or credit risk and can position in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of countries that are not printing too much money," Michael Hasenstab, portfolio manager at Franklin Templeton Fixed Income Group, who manages $150 billion in global fixed income assets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0730 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        79.60          77.07       -3.18\par  Sing dlr        1.2111         1.2052       -0.49\par  Taiwan dlr      28.910         28.938       +0.10\par  Korean won     1061.50        1060.40       -0.10\par  Baht             29.78          29.72       -0.20\par  Peso             42.34          42.23       -0.26\par  Rupiah         8485.00        8475.00       -0.12\par  Rupee            44.43          44.31       -0.27\par  Ringgit         2.9780         2.9650       -0.44\par  Yuan            6.4381         6.4341       -0.06\par  Change so far in 2011\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        79.60          81.15       +1.95\par  Sing dlr        1.2111         1.2820       +5.85\par  Taiwan dlr      28.910         30.368       +5.04\par  Korean won     1061.50        1134.80       +6.91\par  Baht             29.78          30.14       +1.21\par  Peso             42.34          43.84       +3.54\par  Rupiah         8485.00        9005.00       +6.13\par  Rupee            44.43          44.70       +0.61\par  Ringgit         2.9780         3.0820       +3.49\par  Yuan            6.4381         6.5897       +2.35\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please click\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Double click on brackets for following items: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2      Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia \tab \par Malaysian ringgit   Indonesian rupiah  \tab \par Singapore dollar    Thai baht          \tab \par Taiwan dollar       Hong Kong dollar 