\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso at 2-mth high on policy view; won near 34-mth peak\b0\par\par\uc2 1,173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2011\par 04:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Peso up on macro funds, stop-loss dlr sales; BSP steps back\par \par \uc2  * Exporters, stock flows lift won; no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen\par \par \uc2  * Real money accounts support emerging Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Updates with text, prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 6 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso hit a two-month high on Wednesday on views that the country may use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight inflation and the South Korean won flirted with a nearby 34-month peak as there was no sign Seoul was buying dollars.\par \par \uc2  Demand by real money accounts lifted most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggesting inflows to the region may continue over the medium term after the dame kind of investors cut exposure to the region last month.\par \par \uc2  The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BSP) was spotted buying dollars, but they appeared to just slow down the peso's strength, not to defend a certain level, dealers said, after data on Tuesday showed the country's price pressures have been greater than previously reported. \par \par \uc2  "This morning BSP gave the cue when they stepped aside at  43.00. So BSP \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  more like leaning against the wind to limit the speed rather than a committed line in the sand," said Saktiandi Supaat, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Research at Maybank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  "Imported inflation seems to be a focus for now and using PHP to restrain it," he said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could still substnaitally contain the appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Still, he sees the peso seen strengthening past this year's high of 42.635 per dollar by the end of August, barring no external shocks or line in the sand by BSP.\par \par \uc2  This year, unlike before, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities have allowed their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stregnthen in order to fight inflation, especially prices pressure from imports, although they have been spotted buying dollars to slow the gains.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been seen just as efforts to contain gains, not to reverse a market trend or to defend certain levels, dealers said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which dealers said had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month, was not spotted buying dollars on Wednesday, despite heightening caution over their steps as the won threatened to touch a 34-month high hit on Monday.\par \par \uc2  Seoul has pledged to focus policy on stabilising prices and there has been speculation among traders that the government was allowing the won's appreciation as a way to cushion imported inflation as overall consumer inflation stays stubbornly above the upper ceiling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target.\par \par \uc2  The stance, which most Asian policymakers have taken, is seen supporting emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , along with inflows to the region that has stronger economic fundamentals than developed markets have.\par \par \uc2  The regional units are expected to keep enjoying investment flows, although these may dip on concerns over the euro zone's debt crisis and a slowing global economy, analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2  "The market remains happy to sell USD/Asia bounces. We continue to see net equity inflows, perhaps a fresh quarter is seeing new money get put to work," said \uc2 Westpac\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Jonathan Cavenagh in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  PESO\par \par \uc2  The peso  gained up to 0.5 percent to 42.83 per dollar, the strongest since May 4 on macro funds' demand and stop-loss dollar sales.\par \par \uc2  One-year dollar/peso non-deliverable forwards (NDFs)\par \par \uc2 also slid 0.4 percent to 43.170, the lowest since June 10, catching up with the spot move.\par \par \uc2  Interbank speculators had built dollar-long positions on views that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would defend the 43.00 line for the spot, but they had to clear those positions when no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted at that level.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen at 42.90 and 42.85 later, but it was seen trying to slow the peso's strength, not drawing any line in the sand, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  Still, some dealers feel the peso may experience some near-term corrections because investors appeared to hold dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2  "The market is now short," said a European bank dealer in Manila, adding dollar/peso may find a support around 42.85 for now.\par \par \uc2  The 14-day dollar/peso Relative Strength Index (RSI) fell to 34.55, the lowest since May 2 when the index indicated the pair was in oversold territory.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  Demand linked to foreign investors' stock purchases and bids by exporters such as shipbuilders lifted the won \par \par \uc2 closer toward a 34-month high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2  The authorities were not seen in the market, dealers said, although caution over their dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  grew.\par \par \uc2  "The current mood is 'sell (dollar/won) on rallies.' It looks too speedy, but we are on the way to find a level that reflects the authorities' determination with the focus on inflation," said a local bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  "I think we need to go cautiously to the level which they defend and attract importers. To me, it looks like 1,050-1,060 (per dollar)."\par \par \uc2  The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to head to a firm resistance of 1,057, the dollar/won's high on July 2, 2008, days before the pair fell below the 1,000 line.\par \par \uc2  Foreign investors extended stock buying for a sixth straight session.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0830 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par Japan yen        80.92          81.08       +0.20\par Sing dlr        1.2273         1.2287       +0.11\par Taiwan dlr      28.839         28.801       -0.13\par Korean won     1063.20        1066.30       +0.29\par Baht             30.45          30.47       +0.07\par Peso             42.89          43.06       +0.38\par Rupiah         8532.00        8535.00       +0.04\par Rupee            44.45          44.43       -0.06\par Ringgit         3.0080         3.0070       -0.03\par Yuan            6.4666         6.4676       +0.02\par Change so far in 2011\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par Japan yen        80.92          81.15       +0.28\par Sing dlr        1.2273         1.2820       +4.46\par Taiwan dlr      28.839         30.368       +5.30\par Korean won     1063.20        1134.80       +6.73\par Baht             30.45          30.14       -1.02\par Peso             42.89          43.84       +2.21\par Rupiah         8532.00        9005.00       +5.54\par Rupee            44.45          44.70       +0.56\par Ringgit         3.0080         3.0820       +2.46\par Yuan   