\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea end-Apr  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves at record high amid  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk\b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2011\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds background)\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, May 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves leapt by the most in nine months during April, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Tuesday, with the sharp increase underpinning market talk of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the won's gains. \par \par \uc2  The reserves added $8.58 billion to $307.20 billion as of end-April, their highest ever, versus $298.62 billion at the end of March, the Bank of Korea said in a statement.\par \par \uc2  It was the biggest monthly gain since an $11.74 billion rise in July 2010 and compared with a $0.95 billion rise in March.\par \par \uc2  A stronger euro and pound boosted the translated value of dollar-denominated assets, together with investment income, it added. Non-dollar assets represented 36 percent of the reserves at the end of last year.\par \par \uc2  Local authorities have been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to control the pace of the won's gains, only to be outweighed by heavy dollar offers from exporters thanks to booming overseas shipments.    \par \par \uc2  The won  gained 2.35 percent to the dollar in April, bringing its year-to-date gain to 6 percent to 32-month highs as of the end of last month.\par \par \uc2  By comparison, the euro advanced 4.5 percent against the U.S. dollar last month and the pound gained 4.2 percent, according to the Bank of Korea.\par \par \uc2  South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, ranked seventh in the world at the end of March, have logged sequential monthly growth since last December.\par \par \uc2  The won is expected to strengthen further as the dollar has been under pressure on expectations U.S. monetary policy will stay loose. South Korean policymakers are also seen easing their grip on the won to contain imported inflation.\par \par \uc2  South Korea's foreign reserves (in $ billion, at end-month):\par \par \uc2 April   March    Feb      Jan      Dec      Nov      Oct      \par \par \uc2 307.20  298.62   297.67   295.96   291.57   290.23   293.35 \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kim Yeonhee and Lee Soo-jung; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/RESERVES (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110505e752001i6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
