\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-S. Korean inflation below expectation, but BOK hike seen\b0\par\par\uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2011\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * April CPI up 4.2 percent yr/yr, under forecasts\par \par \uc2 * Food prices post monthly decline\par \par \uc2 * Analysts still see further tightening, but PMI, CPI may ease pressures\par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comment on PMI)\par \par \uc2 By Kim Yeonhee and Chang Tae-Min\par \par \uc2 May 2 (Reuters) - South Korean inflation was lower than expected in April as food prices fell sharply, easing pressure on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike interest rates, although economists said they still expected a 25 basis point rise this month.\par \par \uc2 The consumer price index (CPI) rose by 4.2 percent in April from a year ago, less than the 4.4 percent expected in a Reuters poll and it eased from a 29-month high of 4.7 percent in March. Core CPI climbed 3.2 percent year-on-year, down from a 3.3 percent rise in March.\par \par \uc2 Fresh food prices fell by 3.8 percent from the prior month and were up 7.7 percent from a year earlier, a sharp fall from the 19 percent year-on-year rise recording in March.\par \par \uc2 MOST WORRISOME\par \par \uc2 A recent Reuters poll showed economists expected the Bank of Korea to raise its benchmark rate to 3.50 percent by the end of the year from 3.0 percent at present.\par \par \uc2 "It is unlikely that CPI will go back to the three percent level in the near future... What is most worrisome is petroleum product prices," a Bank of Korea official, who could not be named, told Reuters after the CPI release.\par \par \uc2 The government has sought to put a lid on price rises by asking petrol refiners to cut prices and has acted to limit increases in tuition fees.\par \par \uc2 While the Bank of Korea has hiked rates from a record low of 2.0 percent in July 2010, it has been criticised for not getting ahead of the curve on inflation. A recent survey showed that consumers expected inflation over the next 12 months to be 4 percent, at the top end of the Bank of Korea's target range. [ID:nL3E7FQ1HD]\par \par \uc2 "Inflation will ease for the time being, but it is unlikely to drop sharply given high product prices. It will stay above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target," said Goh Yoo-Sun, an economist at \uc2 Daewoo Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 EXPORTS BOOM, DOMESTIC DEMAND WEAK\par \par \uc2 While South Korea's exporters are booming, with exports up 26.6 percent in April from a year ago, the domestic economy is ailing and the government has been forced to bail out construction companies amid weak domestic demand. [ID:nL3E7G100X] [ID:nFT02N]\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Hyundai , the country's largest carmaker, said it sold 380,574 cars overseas in April versus 60,073 in Korea.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HSBC\uc2 /Markit purchasing managers' index (PMI) for the manufacturing sector fell to its lowest level since November last year at a seasonally adjusted 51.69 in April from 52.84 in March, according to data released on Monday, largely down to a stronger won which depressed imported and component prices, said Hana Daetoo Daetoo Securities economist So Jae-yong.\par \par \uc2 The weaker PMI may give the Bank of Korea some room on interst rates, \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's co-head of Asian research Frederic Neumann said.\par \par \uc2 "This (the weaker PMI), in part, may be attributed to supply chain disruptions from Japan, although a broader trade cycle slowdown is probably also at work here. Fortunately, for the Bank of Korea, both input and output price pressures are easing a little which may give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  a little more time before tightening further," he said.\par \par \uc2 Data released last week showed that the construction sector shrank 6.1 percent in the first quarter of this year. [ID:nL3E7FQ0RZ]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to staunch a rising won , which is a threat to exporters. They recently announced measures to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives positions and are set to announce more.\par \par \uc2 The won strengthened on Monday, largely on the back of Sunday's export data and was at 1,066.9 to the dollar by 0104 GMT, stronger than Friday's close of 1,071.5.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kim Yeonhee; Additional reporting by Hyunjoo Jin and Yerim Kim; Writing by David Chance; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner and Richard Borsuk)\par \par \uc2 KOREA/INFLATION (UPDATE 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110502e7520002c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
