\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rises gather momentum after Fed;  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  cited\b0\par\par\uc2 1,197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2011\par 05:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Sing dlr at record high; rupiah at 7-yr peak\par \par \uc2 * Won hits 32-mth high despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , control warning\par \par \uc2 * MAS, BNM, BI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted\par \par \uc2 (Updates with prices, snippets)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, April 28 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gathered upside momentum, touching milestones against the dollar on Thursday after the Federal Reserve signalled it would not hurry to tighten policy, cementing expectations for further fund flows into Asia.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar hit a fresh record high against the greenback and is seen as technically the most overbought since October last year when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened its trading band for the first time since after Sept. 11, 2001 attacks on the United States.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities from many Asian countries including Singapore and \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check strength in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but they moved dollar bids lower in line with overall gains in the regional units, dealers said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players, such as exporters, did not miss out on buying emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dips that resulted from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve's first-ever press conference "appeared merely to confirm the market's view that the Fed will complete its QE2 programme and thereafter maintain ultra-loose monetary policy for the foreseeable future. For now at least, there appeared little to trouble USD bears," said Callum Henderson, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research with Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "The market is clearly short USD, but with USD fundamentals remaining very weak -- weak growth recovery, zero policy rates, high unemployment, rate hikes outside the US, and the terms of trade impact from high oil -- that remains the way to go."\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Chairman Ben Bernanke signaled that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in no rush to scale back its support for the economy with the labour market still in a "very, very deep hole." [ID:nN26291565]\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have risen on growing appetite for higher yields, as regional policymakers fight inflation amid economic fundamentals that are stronger than elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Abundant global liquidity also helped them as investors have piled into Asian stocks and bonds.\par \par \uc2 "Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' gains are really speedy, especially after Bernanke appeared not to have any will to lift the dollar," said Jeong My-young, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist of Samsung Futures in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 Investors appeared long on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, but they saw little risks of massive dollar short-covering for the moment.\par \par \uc2 "Bernanke seems to be rather happy with holding off any tightening move even after completing QE2," said Andy Ji, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist and economist at \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "The Fed thinks both core inflation and inflation expectation are well anchored. So in the short-term, risks of dollar-short cover have diminished somewhat, at least for the next month."\par \par \uc2 Still, more gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may come slowly on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and given market positions, some dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Ji expects regional central banks to intensify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts along with some forms of capital controls.\par \par \uc2 Seoul warned that it may impose fresh capital controls after data showed short-term foreign borrowing in March jumped the most in 27 months amid expectations for further gains in the won \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nL3E7FR5CF]\par \par \uc2 "From here, we should play short-term because risk of a jump(in USD/AXJ) is high with too many short positions," said a senior dealer in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2 The dollar/Singapore dollar's 14-day Relative Strength Index (RSI) fell to 16.7, the weakest since Oct. 14 last year when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore widened the trading band for the city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar/ringgit 14-day RSI slid to 14.9, the lowest since May 2007, indicating the pair are oversold.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won strengthened to as firm as 1,071.0 per dollar in Seoul, the strongest since August 2008, and its one-month non-deliverable forward (NDF) also shrank to the lowest since that same month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were spotted buying dollars to stem gains in the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said a firmer won had had little impact exports on so far and domestic companies would be able to bear the levels. [ID:nL3E7FS00H]\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The rupiah hit a seven-year high against the dollar with strong follow-through demand for Indonesia's new dollar bond.\par \par \uc2 In one of the biggest deals in the dollar space from Asia-Pacific, Jakarta's $2.5 billion medium-term note offering this week was nearly 3 times oversubscribed, with half the issue snapped up by U.S. investors. [ID:nIFR75cDT4]\par \par \uc2 The rupiah firmed to as strong as 8,572, the strongest since April 2004.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollara, initially from 8,600 up to 8,610, but pulled back its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lines.\par \par \uc2 A European bank dealer in Jakarta said Bank Indonesia would allow more appreciation as it is a regional trend.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Central banks of Singapore and Malaysia were spotted buying dollars to slow down strength in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which were seen as more overbought than others.\par \par \uc2 But they also lowered levels of U.S. dollar bids in line with a slide in the greenback, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The MAS was spotted buying the U.S. dollar from 1.2280, but the Singapore dollar strengthened to as firm as 1.2250.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0710 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        81.56          82.17       +0.75\par  Sing dlr        1.2258         1.2296       +0.31\par  Taiwan dlr      28.703         28.900       +0.69\par  Korean won     1071.10        1079.50       +0.78\par  Baht             29.80          29.96       +0.54\par  Peso             42.95          43.22       +0.62\par  Rupiah         8575.00        8625.00       +0.58\par  Rupee            44.32     