\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S.Korea GDP expands on export boom despite builders' woes\b0\par\par\uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2011\par 01:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Q1 GDP growth of 1.4 pct fastest since Q2 2010\par \par \uc2 * Sustained slump in domestic demand a headache\par \par \uc2 * Government working on steps to help builders\par \par \uc2 (Recasts throughout with minister, economist quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Yoo Choonsik and Kim Yeonhee\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, April 27 (Reuters) - South Korea's economy grew at its fastest pace in three quarters in January-March thanks to robust exports, but sluggish domestic demand is posing a dilemma for policymakers who are struggling to balance sustainable growth against mounting inflation risks.\par \par \uc2 Foreign trade contributed nearly 90 percent of the 1.4 percent quarterly growth in gross domestic product (GDP) in the first quarter of 2011, while the hard-hit domestic construction sector contracted 6.1 percent from the prior quarter, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Wednesday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a rising won \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect its exporters and is considering measures to boost the domestic construction industry ahead of a flurry of elections next year.\par \par \uc2 Overall robust economic growth will allow the Bank of Korea to raise interest rates as early as next month for a fifth time since its current tightening cycle started last July, as it attempts to contain inflation that is running way ahead of its 4 percent target ceiling.\par \par \uc2 However, it is expectd to remain cautious about the extent of further hikes as higher borrowing costs could act as both a brake on economic growth and add to household debt in South Korea, which is already among the highest in the 34-member OECD (Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development).\par \par \uc2 "I don't think the government will come up with measures strong enough to turn everything around, mainly due to concerns about heavy household sector debt," said Kim Yoon-gee, who heads the Daishin Economic Research Institute.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For full table, double-click [ID:nL3E7FQ0RZ]\par \par \uc2 For analysts' comments, double-click [ID:nL3E7FQ18L]\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 First-quarter growth was the fastest since the second quarter of 2010 and the a ninth consecutive quarterly expansion, coming in marginally above a 1.3 percent increase forecast in a Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 Net exports lifted GDP by 1.2 percent while weak construction spending pulled it down 1.1 percent, Bank of Korea data showed, indicating Asia's fourth-largest economy would have expanded only 0.2 percent if not for exports.\par \par \uc2 Over a year earlier, GDP in the first quarter rose 4.2 percent, compared with the market's median forecast of 4.1 percent and following a revised 4.7 percent annual gain in the final quarter of 2010.\par \par \uc2 HEAVY HOUSEHOLD DEBT LIMITS ROOM FOR POLICY RATE HIKES\par \par \uc2 Some market watchers fear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already behind the curve in fighting inflation, and has been staying its hand on more aggressive rate rises out of concern that they could stifle growth and potentially create a household debt crisis in Asia's fourth-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 "I expect the BOK to raise rates in May. Today's GDP data is positive (when) considering economic jitters, while April exports are expected to be robust," said Lee Sung-kwon, chief economist at Shinhan Investment Corp.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea (BOK) has raised its policy interest rate by a total of 1 percentage point from record-low 2 percent in four steps between July last year and March this year. It held the rate steady this month and next reviews policy on May 13.\par \par \uc2 With the depressed construction sector weighing on domestic demand, the country's land minister promised measures to help buidlers at a closed-door meeting with construction industry leaders, state media reported.\par \par \uc2 Land, Transport and Maritime Minister Chung Jong-hwan did not elaborate on what steps the government may take, but industry leaders urged the government to help roll over their maturing loans and sought easier lending regulations, state broadcaster KBS reported.\par \par \uc2 The government also is trying to reduce the risks of small savings banks which are heavily exposed to the construction sector with a package of bailouts from healthy banks. [ID:nL3E7FQ0F6] [ID:nL3E7FI07E]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed the construction industry's output shrank by a seasonally adjusted 6.1 percent in the first three months of the year from the preceding quarter, the fourth consecutive quarterly decline and the worst in 13 years.\par \par \uc2 Even though the country's turbo-charged export sector goes from strength-to-strengtt, driven by booming demand for such goods as cars built by \uc2 Hyundai Motor Corp\uc2  , the average South Korean consumer is deeply indebted, crimping domestic expansion.\par \par \uc2 Official data shows South Korea's household debts stand nearly 1.5 times their annual disposable income, next only to Britain among OECD member economies.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by David Chance and Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/GDP (UPDATE 2, PIX)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110426e74q001cq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
