\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 838 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2011\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIA CENTRAL BANKS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AGAIN AS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  EXTEND RALLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar continued to sell off sharply in Asia Thursday, prompting central banks in South Korea and Malaysia to try to curb the surge in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to long-term highs by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the second day running. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SOUTH KOREA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO LAUNCH 2ND ROUND OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  INSPECTIONS AT BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean authorities said Thursday they'll launch a second round of inspections of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions at banks, focusing on activity in the overseas non-deliverable forward market. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 1Q PPI STRONG, BUT SOARING DOLLAR TO STALL RBA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Soaring prices for fuel, electricity and food drove Australian producer price inflation higher in the first quarter, with little offset from a high Australian dollar, economists said Thursday. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 1ST-QUARTER BUSINESS CONFIDENCE RISES; CONDITIONS FLAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Confidence levels among Australian businesses rose sharply during the first quarter as managers put the worst of January's record flooding in Queensland behind them, but still-soft trading and profits meant business conditions remained flat, according to an industry survey released Thursday. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA FINANCE MINISTER IDENTIFIES A$465M SPENDING CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Finance Minister Penny Wong said Thursday the government will seek to cut the costs of the day-to-day running of government by lifting the so-called efficiency dividend to create savings worth A$465 million in the budget to be announced on May 10. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: LONG-TERM RATES TO RISE IF FISCAL CONFIDENCE LOST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa said Thursday long-term interest rates could rise if investors lose confidence in the government's efforts to tackle the country's worsening fiscal condition. (published 0320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ NISHIMURA SEES POST-QUAKE SUPPLY PROBLEMS EASING AFTER AUTUMN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura said Thursday he expects supply-side problems caused by the March 11 earthquake to ease after the autumn, though the nation's economy is expected to stay "under strong downward pressure" for some time. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA: EXPECT NEW YUAN FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT RULE TO BE IN PLACE IN 2H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expects a new rule covering the use of the yuan for foreign direct investment to be in place in the second half of this year, the de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Deputy Chief Executive Peter Pang told reporters on the sidelines of a conference Thursday. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA MOF: INFLATION TO PEAK AT 5.5%-5.6% MID-2011 - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rise in China's consumer price index is expected to peak at 5.5% to 5.6% in the middle of this year, state-run Shanghai Securities News reported Thursday citing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official Ma Shuanyou. (published 0113 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA IMPOSES ON ANTI-DUMPING MEASURES ON OPTICAL FIBER IMPORTS FROM US, EU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Ministry of Commerce will levy anti-dumping duties ranging from 4.7% to 29.1% depending on the extent of dumping on imports of a type of optical fiber from the U.S. and the E.U., according to the ministry's final ruling on the matter. (published 0307 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ADB INSTITUTE KAWAI: CAPITAL INFLOWS CONTROL NEEDED IN ASIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian countries continue to face the risk of capital inflows and controls on such flows are needed, the head of the Asian Development Bank Institute said Thursday. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PAKISTAN TO RAISE OVER $500 MLN FROM OGDC CONVERTIBLE BONDS; NAME BANKS EARLY MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pakistan will raise more than $500 million from the long-planned sale of dollar-denominated convertible bonds of state-run Oil & Gas Development Co. this year and may use part of the proceeds to service the country's mounting external debt, a person familiar with the matter said late Wednesday. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: GUANGZHOU R&F PROPERTIES SELLS TWO-TRANCHE YUAN, DOLLAR BOND; TOTAL SIZE $550 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Guangzhou R&F Properties Co. has sold a three-year CNY2.612 billion offshore yuan-denominated bond at par with a 7.00% yield, and a five-year $150 million U.S. dollar bond at par with a 10.875% yield, a person familiar with the deal said Thursday. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CENTURY TOKYO LEASING CORP SELLS 3-YEAR CNY200 MLN OFFSHORE YUAN BOND AT PAR TO YIELD 2.70% - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Century Tokyo Leasing Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  has sold a CNY200 million three-year offshore yuan bond at par to yield 2.700%, a person familiar with the deal said Thursday. (published 0252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ORIX CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  SELLS $400 MLN 2016 TAP TO YIELD 4.523% - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial services group \f28 \uc2 \f2 ORIX Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has sold a $400 million tap of its existing note issue due Jan. 12, 2016 at 101.997 to yield 4.523%, with a spread of 240 basis points over comparable Treasurys, a person familiar with the matter said Thursday. (published 0307 GMT) [ 21-04-11 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110421e74l000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
