\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr, rupee up on fund flows\b0\par\par\uc2 888 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2010\par 04:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Taiwan dlr hit fresh 3-wk high; rupee up 0.4 pct\par \par \uc2  * Won turns higher to hit 2-wk high\par \par \uc2  * Seen staying firm; euro woes may cap gains\par \par \uc2  By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar and the Indian  rupee rose against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday amid continuous  foreign fund inflows, leading overall gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The South Korean won also turned higher to hit a two-week  high on exporters' demand for settlements and as investors  cleared dollar-long positions to stop losses.\par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to remain firm as investors  hunt for more assets in the region, although sustained worries  about the euro zone's debt problems may limit the gains,  analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2  "An overall bullish trend remains intact. But it is not a  time to add long positions in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively  on the lingering euro zone woes," said Jeong My-young, a  \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Samsung Futures Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Financial markets in Malaysia and Indonesia were closed for  holidays.\par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar hit a fresh high against the  dollar in over three weeks on sustained offshore fund inflows,  but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to curb its  strength.\par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to as firm as 30.080 per  dollar, the strongest since Nov. 12.\par \par \uc2  The dollar/Taiwan dollar returned to above 30.10 by the  \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's activity.\par \par \uc2  Taiwan's exports rose 21.8 percent in November from a year  earlier, compared with Reuters' forecast of 19.75 percent gain.  [ID:nTPV002232]\par \par \uc2  Stronger-than-expected November consumer inflation made a  rate increase later this month almost inevitable, with some  suggestion markets could see a 25 bps hike despite economists'  fascination with solely the core number. [ID:nTOE6B504O]\par \par \uc2  RUPEE\par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee extended its winning streak to a sixth  session, firming 0.4 percent to 44.78 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2  "44.80 is a key level to watch out for. If this level holds  and we get back above 45.10, then we could see 45.50-45.70  levels again," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with a  private bank.\par \par \uc2  "If we break 44.80, then we could see 44.50-44.20 levels  and  then a move back up to 45," he added.\par \par \uc2  Dealers expect importers to come in to buy dollars around  44.80.\par \par \uc2  Foreign funds had bought $638 million worth of shares over  last week, latest data shows, taking net investments to a  record  $29.3 billion in 2010, on top of the $17.5 billion purchased  last  year.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won hit a two-week high against the dollar as  exporters chased it for settlements and as a rebound in the  euro prompted investors to clear long-dollar positions to stop  losses.\par \par \uc2  Foreign investors turned to net buyers of local shares, further supporting the won .\par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to strengthen past a  psychological  resistance line of 1,130 per dollar on caution over possible  \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2  The won is expected to stay in a tight range despite strong  investor appetite for the country's assets as the euro is seen  vulnerable with European policymakers bickering over how to  tackle the region's debt crisis. [ID:nLDE6B51VW]\par \par \uc2  "It looks difficult for the won to keep rising further as  we  did not find concrete solutions in the euro zone yet," said  Jung  Kyung-parl, head of market analysis team of KEB Futures.    \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0800 GMT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen        82.59          82.64       +0.06\tab \par  Sing dlr        1.3037         1.3045       +0.06\tab \par  Taiwan dlr      30.101         30.625       +1.74\tab \par  Korean won     1132.70        1133.20       +0.04\tab \par  Baht             29.98          30.04       +0.20\tab \par  Peso             43.56          43.75       +0.45\tab \par  Rupee            44.78          44.96       +0.40\tab \par  Yuan            6.6474         6.6484       +0.02\tab \par  \tab \par  Change so far in 2010\tab \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\tab \par  Japan yen        82.59          92.90      +12.48\tab \par  Sing dlr        1.3037         1.4053       +7.79\tab \par  Taiwan dlr      30.101         32.030       +6.41\tab \par  Korean won     1132.70        1164.50       +2.81\tab \par  Baht             29.98          33.32      +11.14\tab \par  Peso             43.56          46.20       +6.07\tab \par  Rupiah         9005.00        9420.00       +4.61\tab \par  Rupee            44.78          46.54       +3.94\tab \par  Ringgit         3.1430         3.4220       +8.88\tab \par  Yuan            6.6474         6.8270       +2.70\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  \tab \par  (Additional reporting by Swati Bhat in MUMBAI and Peter \par Whitley \tab \par from IFR M