\par\par \b \uc2 Q+A-Will Japan  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  again?\b0\par\par\uc2 964 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2010\par 12:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 22 (Reuters) - The dollar has fallen within spitting distance of its post-war record low against the yen and market players say Japanese authorities might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if it falls sharply, after they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September.\par \par \uc2 But there is a growing impression among some traders that, with a debate globally about competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation and Japan's recent criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tokyo may not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, even though its policy makers say they might.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has lost 3.5 percent on the yen since the end of August and 13 percent so far this year, despite 2.1 trillion yen or $25 billion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold across the board after the Federal Reserve signalled it was ready to ease policy again.\par \par \uc2 The dollar dipped to its lowest in 15 years this week, to 80.84 yen <JPY=>. It has recovered above 81.00 yen but the market is jittery about the possibility that Japan will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grinds down towards its 1995 post-war low of 79.75 yen.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Q+A on Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capacity        [ID:nTOE68S07S]\par  Q+A on unsterilised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2             [ID:nTOE68G02P]\par  Graphic on trade weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 fx\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :   \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/qun86p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/qun86p}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tensions map:          \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/jec96p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/jec96p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  PDF report on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :       \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/gez77p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/gez77p}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WHAT MIGHT PROMPT JAPAN TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AGAIN?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan acts on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and those who think it might step back in say it could do so if there were a rapid rise in the yen specifically, rather than a general drop in the dollar, possibly through 80 yen per dollar, and accompanied by a sharp drop in the Nikkei <.N225> share average.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If yen crosses such as the euro/yen and Australian dollar/yen rates remain reasonably stable, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen as less likely. But general yen strength could change the equation, especially if it is being driven by a build up of speculative positions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some traders say a sharp fall in Japanese share prices could alarm the authorities and prompt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . If the Nikkei falls below a 16-month low near 8,800 hit in early September, the Japanese government may feel more pressed to act.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WON'T THE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WARS DEBATE STOP THEM?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The debate makes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more difficult, when China is under pressure to allow more rapid appreciation of the yuan, and this is one reason why some in the market think the likelihood is diminishing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan escaped overt criticism from its G7 counterparts for its Sept. 15 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the only confirmed bout so far. But behind the scenes it got heavy criticism from the Europeans, which has now made it very difficult for Tokyo to justify \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again, a G7 source told Reuters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed the tone of Japanese policy makers' comments changed after the October IMF and G7 meetings in Washington. Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda was at pains to stress that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was aimed at stopping excessive moves from hurting the economy, rather than the start of a big, long campaign aimed at targeting a specific \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Noda then criticised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep down its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying Seoul's leadership of the G20 would come under question due to its regular \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a barb some analysts took to mean: "If we can't do it, then neither can you."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By criticising South Korea, Noda also did not sound to some like a finance minister considering immediate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SO WHAT'S THE AUTHORITIES' STRATEGY?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The strategy is hard to fathom at this stage because of the politics involved and because the only confirmed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past six years is the Sept. 15 action, so the market does not have a lot to go on.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Levels the market thought might be lines in the sand have been and gone, with the next potential one at 80 yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While at first some thought Sept. 15 marked the start of a longer campaign, now it may be that the authorities keep the action down to a few opportunistic occasions to counter rapid yen moves and remind the market of the two-way risk.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the meantime, policy makers keep up a steady stream of verbal reminders that they will act decisively when needed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HOW FAR IS THE YEN LIKELY TO RISE?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If no \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  occurs and the yen strengthens through 80 per dollar and then 79.75, some see it moving up to 78-76 per dollar to start with. Daisuke Uno, chief strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 , told Reuters in September that his personal forecast was for the yen to reach 50 next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Reuters poll in early October showed a median forecast of 88 yen per dollar in six months' time and 92 yen in a year. <FXJPY>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A dollar drop below 80 yen would likely turn that level into resistance which the greenback could struggle to break at first.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the options market, implied volatilities are subdued, suggesting that option market players expect the yen's rise will be slow, with one-month volatility at 11.5 percent\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But a trader at a Japanese bank also noted there has been buying in longer-dated dollar puts/yen calls, such as six months and nine months, with strike prices far below the record low of 79.75 yen, suggesting expectations of a deeper fall in the dollar. (Reporting by Masayuki Kitano, Hideyuki Sano, Leika Kihara and Charlotte Cooper; Editing by Edmund Klamann)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Q+A)|LANGEN|J|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|Z|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101022e6am000wk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
