rs judged the Fed will succeed in pushing inflation higher. Meanwhile, ECB President Trichet over the weekend said a majority of the governing council did not share the view of Bundesbank's Weber that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should stop buying bonds of peripheral euro-zone countries. Weber's comments earlier this month had pressured the markets so the latest news flow should ease worries that the ECB is likely to exit its loose monetary stance pretty soon. There is no economic release of note in the euro zone, although US industrial production data are out. December bunds are down 0.05 at 130.67 and the 10-year bund is up at 98.92, yielding 2.373%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0635 GMT [Dow Jones] HK short-selling volume down 2.1% at HK$3.283 billion, 5.5% of total market volume vs 5.2% at Friday's half-day, suggesting bears not stepping up bets despite HSI in 2-day losing streak. ICBC (1398.HK) leads with HJK$441.74 million, followed by A50 China Tracker (2823.HK) with HK$271.81 million. Next come \uc2 HSBC\uc2  (0005.HK) with HK$228.58 million, Hutchison (0013.HK) with HK$220.43 million, HKEx (0388.HK) with HK$177.81 million. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0635 GMT [Dow Jones] Switzerland's economy is performing well, compared with its European neighbors, particularly in the labor market, according to \uc2 McKinsey & Co\uc2 . "While Switzerland wasn't directly covered in the EU-15-focused report, it's deeply linked to the European economy," it says. "In terms of the reform agenda laid out, Switzerland shows very good performance in the labor market, with one of the lowest unemployment rates in Europe," it notes. "The employment rate of older workers was a very high 68 percent, and it also scores well on innovation metrics like triadic patents per capita, outperforming Germany in 2007 by about 50%," it says. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0629 GMT [Dow Jones] Much-awaited opening of Mumbai's new