icularly in the labor market, according to \uc2 McKinsey & Co\uc2 . "While Switzerland wasn't directly covered in the EU-15-focused report, it's deeply linked to the European economy," it says. "In terms of the reform agenda laid out, Switzerland shows very good performance in the labor market, with one of the lowest unemployment rates in Europe," it notes. "The employment rate of older workers was a very high 68 percent, and it also scores well on innovation metrics like triadic patents per capita, outperforming Germany in 2007 by about 50%," it says. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0629 GMT [Dow Jones] Much-awaited opening of Mumbai's new diamond trading hub, Bharat Diamond Bourse, finally happened Sunday. Building $250 million trading hub took 18 years and twice the amount of money expected after repeated delays due to everything from structural modifications to battles between leading diamond merchants to flooding from torrential rains. Anoop Mehta, president of bourse, said exchange, which has 2,500 offices, four walk-in vaults, 24,500 safe deposit boxes and a 6,200 sq ft trading floor, is world's largest. He said nearly $18 billion worth of diamonds exported from India during last fiscal year; he is hoping new trading hub will bring more international diamond traders to India's financial capital. "We haven't had foreigners coming here for trading and manufacturing of their diamonds because we just didn't have infrastructure that was at par with Israel or Antwerp," Mehta said. "Now that we have the facilities, I am certain that more diamond traders will be encouraged to set up offices in India." See: =WSJ BLOG/India Real Time: Mumbai's New Diamond Market Opens at Last (arlene.chang@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0628 GMT [Dow Jones] ASIAN SUMMARY: Regional markets mostly lower; Nikkei flat, S&P/ASX off 0.8%, Shanghai Composite +0.5%, HSI down 1.0%, STI down 0.1%, KLCI down 0.4%, NZX-50 +0.2%, Kospi off 1.4%, Taiex 1.8% lower, SET slipped 0.3%, Sensex down 1.