of G20 finance ministers, central bankers in Gyeongju, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears out of question this week ahead of the G20, as Japanese authorities would not want to be that provocative," says senior dealer at major Japanese bank. While Finance Minister Noda said Friday Japan would again "take decisive steps when necessary" to curb excessive exchange rate moves, "regardless of whether there are Group of Seven or Group of 20 meetings," dealer says current pace of USD/JPY decline has not been excessive. Pair last 81.16 vs earlier high 81.53.(andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0621 GMT [Dow Jones] Bullish AUD/USD traders looking to enhance returns in range above parity consider overlaying 3-month 1x2 AUD call/USD put spread, says Dow Jones CommentaryPlus senior analyst Russell Floyd; suggests buying A$10 million Jan 18 0.9985 AUD call/USD put for 192 USD pips, selling A$20 million Jan 18 1.0300 AUD call/USD put for 96 USD pips for zero upfront premium. For those looking to secure profits after strong spot run-up, suggests hedging in range below spot with 1x2 AUD put/USD call spread: buy Jan 18 expiry A$10 million 0.9790 AUD put/USD call for 284 USD pips, sell Jan 18 expiry A$20 million 0.9375 AUD put/USD call for 142 USD pips. See =\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  OPTION VIEWS: Consider Aussie Ratio Spreads Around Parity. (murugesan.suppayyan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0620 GMT [Dow Jones] Some time today, four-member panel set up by India's environment ministry on July 28 expected to submit report on South Korean steelmaker Posco's (005490.SE) Orissa steel plant project. Panel investigating whether project will violate rights of local tribes living on forest land likely to be cleared for $12-billion steel plant's construction, adherence to other environmental regulations. Once report submitted to Ministry of Environment and Forests, yet another panel will discuss it, submit recommendations to environment minister, Jairam Ramesh, whose decision will be guided by committee's recommendation. In August, ministry shot down \uc2 Vedanta Resources\uc2 ' (VED.LN) five-year-old proposal to mine for bauxite. Over weekend, local media reported panel split; could make Ramesh decision trickier. Getting environmental approval for projects has always been tough, time-consuming as requires layers of local, state, federal approvals. But analysts feel Posco project may not meet fate of Vedanta's proposal. Too much riding on it. South Korean government has seriously pushed project with Indian government at highest level. See: =WSJ BLOG/India Real Time: A Judgment Day of Sorts for Posco (arlene.chang@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0615 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan shares end down 1.8% at 8060.54, weighed by weakness in heavyweight exporters on concerns of strong TWD and HTC's (2498.TW) fall on Apple Daily report, citing an unnamed analyst, as saying new Window Mobile 7 handsets have reboot problems, says Taiwan International Securities assistant vice president Andrew Teng. "We may see more consolidation Tuesday as the market has priced in most of the good news. But Taiex should see firm support at 8000 as long-term economic fundamentals remain solid." HTC off 6.9% at NT$624.00, TSMC (2330.TW) off 2.3% at NT$60.50, UMC (2303.TW) off 2.2% at NT$13.35. (lorraine.luk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0614 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 UBS\uc2  is bullish on the weekly outlook for EUR/CHF and sees upside potential to 1.3665 should 1.3494 be breached. On the downside, there is strong technical support at 1.3265 and then at 1.3027, according to \uc2 UBS\uc2  technical analyst Gareth Berry. EUR/CHF at 1.3359 from a previous close at 1.3396. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0606 GMT [Dow Jones] China government will do another serious \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if housing prices rise more than 1% on-month for several consecutive months, says CLSA strategist Andy Rothman. "As long as prices rise in line with nominal urban income - about 1% on-month - the government will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dramatic measures, but we should expect continued efforts to cool speculative buying, which accounts for about 16% of total sales," he says. Adds, over last 5 years, average annual nominal urban income +13% while average house prices +12% per year. Official data shows China property prices +0.5% on-month in September. Rothman says China housing prices unlikely to rise too fast in near future as housing investment, starts and completions all rose rapidly in September, suggesting supply-demand balance will remain healthy. (esther.fung@dowjones.com) [ 10-18-10 0238ET ]\par \par \uc2 0554 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude oil futures down on profit-taking, stronger greenback, says Ken Hasegawa, commodity derivative sales manager at Newedge Japan. "Crude couldn't climb over $84 resistance level last week, so it is now dropping as traders take profits." Oil will continue to take cues from U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, may test $80/bbl soon, Hasegawa adds. November Nymex crude down $0.62 at $80.63--close to 10-day low; hit $80.56/bbl earlier during session. (max.lin@dowjones.com) [ 10-18-10 0238ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101018e6ai00042\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
