\par\par \b \uc2 G20 host S.Korea: protectionism is top concern\b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 17:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 15 (Reuters) - South Korean President Lee Myung-bak, who will chair next month's G20 summit, expressed concern on Friday over the possibility of trade protectionism emerging due to conflicts of national interest.\par \par \uc2 Lee also said there was an urgent need for the Group of 20 major economies to compromise on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Economic imbalances, the falling dollar and pressure on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise are set to dominate meetings in South Korea of G20 finance ministers from Oct. 22 and national leaders from Nov. 11.\par \par \uc2 "What's worrying me the most is that conflicts of interest between countries could develop into trade protectionism," Lee was quoted as saying in a statement from the presidential office.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stand-off ahead of G20           [ID:nLDE69308R]\par Scenarios                                 [ID:nLDE69E01X]\par PDF-Race to the Bottom        \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/gez77p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/gez77p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par Graphic on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tensions  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/deh58p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/deh58p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par Insider TV                 \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyj28p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyj28p}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He did not specifically respond to Japanese criticism of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but his comment on the conflicts of national interests was widely seen as referring to international tension over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The world economy could become more predictable next year once (member economies) reach agreement at the G20 meeting," Lee was quoted as telling economics editors at major local media companies on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Yoon Jeung-hyun, who chairs next week's meetings of finance ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governors from the 20 major economies, also warned earlier in the day against signs of trade protectionism. [ID:nTOE69E00M] (Reporting by Yoo Choonsik; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2 /KOREA-PRESIDENT|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101015e6af0016l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
