\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won up on Japan remarks; govt caution remains\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2010\par 02:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Won up 1 pct on Japan's comments on S.Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Seoul unlikely to change \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance - dealers, analysts\par \par \uc2 * Eyes on c.bank rate meeting on Thursday (Updates to domestic close)\par \par \uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 13 (Reuters) - The won rose against the dollar on Wednesday after Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda complained about \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on rekindled expectations for further easing by the Federal Reserve.\par \par \uc2 Noda said South Korea's leadership of the Group of 20 nations forum could come under question because of its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nTOE69C00G]\par \par \uc2 The comments prompted some expectations that Seoul may scale back dollar purchases, but failed to dispel caution over steps by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to check the won's <KRW=> strength, analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The wariness prevented the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaking through 1,120 per dollar, they added.\par \par \uc2 "Noda's comments reflected Japan's desperation as its more than 2 trillion yen ($24.43 billion) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not work. The Korean authorities are unlikely to change their stance because of the comments," said Kim Jae-eun, an economist at \uc2 Hyundai Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities have yet to comment on Noda's remarks.\par \par \uc2 They were estimated to have bought a combined $13 billion for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Sept. 27 and Oct. 12, according to estimates from traders compiled by IFR Markets. [ID:nSGE69C059]\par \par \uc2 The won ended domestic trade up 1.0 percent against the dollar at 1,120.7 per dollar from Tuesday's domestic close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,131.5.\par \par \uc2 After Noda's comments, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to as firm as 1,117.3.\par \par \uc2 "The won's bullish trend remains intact, but investors just cleared dollar-long positions after the comment. They were reluctant to buy more won," said a local bank dealer. "Players are more focusing on regulation risks, especially after Thailand's move yesterday."\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Thai Finance Minister said the country would impose a 15 percent withholding tax on interest and capital gains earned by foreign investors on Thai bonds, the latest bid by an emerging economy to tame its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nSGE69B0A6]\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold a net 140 billion won ($123.9 million) worth of stocks on the Seoul's main exchange while the benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> closed up 0.43 percent.\par \par \uc2 Investors will be watching the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate setting meeting on Thursday. The Bank of Korea is expected to raise the 7-day repurchase agreement rate by 25 basis points this week, a Reuters poll showed. [ID:nTOE69100L]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                 Close       0015 GMT     Prev close\par  Won             1,120.7    1,121.3/1.6        1,131.5\par  Yen/won    *13.6863/984    13.7011/147    13.8233/362\par  KOSPI          1,876.15       1,875.08       1,868.04\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1=1130.1 Won) (Additional reporting by Lee Soo-jung; Editing by Chris Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101016e6ad00007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
