\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: US To Press  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Issues At IMF--Treasury Official\b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2010\par 18:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds additional official comment, details and background, in the third through ninth, 12th and 13th paragraphs.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Ian Talley and Michael R. Crittenden \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--U.S. officials plan to press their foreign counterparts to avoid interfering in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at this weekend's International Monetary Fund meetings, warning of the potential effect on the global rebalancing efforts.\par \par \uc2 A senior Treasury Department official, speaking to reporters at a briefing, said U.S. officials will stress the need for countries to allow for "market-oriented exchange rates" as part of a broader rebalancing of the world economy.\par \par \uc2 Besides China's undervalued yuan, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Brazil and Tokyo in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have raised \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions, propelling the sensitive issue to the forefront of international talks.\par \par \uc2 The chorus of complaints internationally has grown louder for China to appreciate its undervalued yuan, particularly as Beijing's policy is exacerbating the global imbalance of trade and investment. Turbulence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was taken to a new level after Brazil warned of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, European Economic and Monetary Affairs Commissioner Olli Rehn warned that the euro area's economic recovery may suffer if the euro appreciates against the yuan and other world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Officials in Brussels met with Chinese Prime Minister Wen Jiabao.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Japan's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the yen, the Treasury official implicitly criticized Tokyo for the action as contrary to its commitments to the Group of 20 nations.\par \par \uc2 The official said Japan and others in the G-20 are focused on cultivating a more robust recovery, and that countries with trade surpluses, including Japan and China, have committed to encouraging domestic demand as a bigger engine of growth and so becoming less reliant on exports over time.\par \par \uc2 "Explicitly in those agreements are structural policies as well as ensuring that exchange rates represent market forces," the senior official said.\par \par \uc2 The official said those commitments would be "central to our conversations" at the upcoming IMF meetings.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. believes the IMF should play a more aggressive role in ensuring countries live up to their commitments on exchange-rate policy, the official said, stressing the fund's "very important surveillance mandate."\par \par \uc2 "The IMF has to have an ability to speak forcefully," the official said.\par \par \uc2 While the IMF has labeled the yuan as "substantially undervalued," the IMF has yet to call the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "manipulated," which would ostensibly ratchet up pressure on Beijing to act.\par \par \uc2 Fueling tensions, the U.S. House of Representatives last month approved legislation targeting the yuan that would slap punitive tariffs on imports from countries such as China that have undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The official said the Obama administration shared the underlying concerns addressed by the bill, but was reluctant to say whether the Treasury supported the legislation. Previously, officials have raised concerns about World Trade Organization obligations and the potential political and trade backlash such legislation may engender.\par \par \uc2 The issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of a range of topics finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials are expected to discuss at a series of multi- and bilateral discussions in Washington over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 -By Michael R. Crittenden, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9273; michael.crittenden@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -By Ian Talley, Dow Jones Newswires, 202-862-9285; ian.talley@dowjones.com [ 10-05-10 1219ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101005e6a5000ai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
