 property tightening, should be taken as sign of market's underlying strength. Market volume strong at HK$46.97 billion at interval, doesn't appear index would slide more; week's lowest of 22,109 likely won't troubled. ICBC down 3.2% at HK$5.78, China Overseas Land (0688.HK) tumbles 3.7% to HK$16.20, \uc2 China Resources Land\uc2  (1109.HK) off 4.5% at HK$15.76, but weakness in part offset by rally in Hutchison (0013.HK), big HK developers Cheung Kong (0001.HK), \uc2 SHK Properties\uc2  (0016.HK). Overall, given HSI's about 9% gain in September, "we believe the market will enter a period of consolidation over the next few trading sessions," says \uc2 Celestial Securities\uc2 . (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0429 GMT [Dow Jones] PREVIEW: Hong Kong August retail sales growth likely remained in double digits, but likely slowed vs July on fading base factor. By value, tipped +16.0% on-year in August vs July's +18.9%; by volume +13.2% in August vs July's +16.0%, according to Dow Jones poll of 5 economists. "Domestic demand remains buoyant with the fall in the jobless rate and tourist arrivals continue to be resilient, but the higher base of comparison last year also weighs on the headline figure," Core Pacific-Yamaichi analyst Keith Lo says. \uc2 Bank of East Asia\uc2  economist Paul Tang says retail sales growth likely fell to "high single digits" in 4Q due to higher base of comparison, as city's retail sales returned to growth since September last year. Data due 0830 GMT Monday. (chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0424 GMT [Dow Jones] While central banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Singapore, Thailand and Indonesia were suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets overnight, following confirmed moves by Japan earlier this month, don't expect \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  to do any such thing, say traders and strategists. With surging mining sector, robust banking system, inflation a very real concern, RBA is looking to cool the economy any way it can, with gains in AUD helping \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "If the Aussie dollar wasn't as high as it is, we could see more than one rate hike by the end of the year as it's doing some heavy lifting for the RBA. A high Aussie dollar curbs importers and inflation, creating a dampening affect that is exactly what the RBA wants," says \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  Economist Helen Kevans. AUD/USD last at 0.9670 after hitting 26-month high around 0.9730 overnight. (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com) [ 09-30-10 0141ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100930e69u0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
