\par\par \b \uc2 MONEY TALKS: Fed's Mending Ways May Put Asia In A Bind\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shri Navaratnam   \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires Column   \par \uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2010\par 10:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--As Ben Bernanke maneuvers the Federal Reserve closer to further quantitative easing, Asian policy makers may find themselves bearing some of the pain of keeping the U.S. economy afloat.\par \par \uc2 The Fed made it amply clear this week it is concerned about low inflation--and indeed the risk of deflation--in the U.S. and stands ready to act to fulfil its mandate of promoting maximum employment and price stability.\par \par \uc2 It's likely that Bernanke & Co. will be compelled--unless they are blessed with a sudden and apparently-sustainable improvement in data prints--to embark on another round of monetary loosening. An announcement on QE looks a distinct possibility at the next policy meeting in November.\par \par \uc2 Flooding the market with more U.S. dollars to lower the cost of credit and inflate the economy may be the way to go; in Asia, however, we may see some fallout from the Fed's actions.\par \par \uc2 Further easing from the Fed could send the U.S. dollar down and already-strong Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  up, endangering the region's export-dependent economies.\par \par \uc2 Asian central banks could be forced to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the dollar and temper the impact on exporters. Japan last week was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  massively for the first time in six years, as a surging yen threatened an already-sluggish economic recovery. Other countries in the region, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Singapore and Taiwan, have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Asia will also have to contend with the potential surge in hot money flows to sectors such as housing, heightening the risk of asset price bubbles. With Treasury yields likely to ease on any fresh QE, more investors will turn to Asia for yield.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in the region may lay low for some months on rates, but if they start hiking to curb inflation that will only accentuate rate differentials.\par \par \uc2 Such a scenario will pose a policy dilemma for Asia's central banks. Thailand is already moving to introduce rules to boost capital outflows, while the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it's mulling changes to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations to address a surge in portfolio investments that has buoyed the peso.\par \par \uc2 With Asia already battling rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the last thing it needs is for the Fed to further frustrate the situation.\par \par \uc2 Still, the way the cards are stacked up, policy makers in the region will probably be the first to acknowledge that the Fed cannot sit on its hands and risk deflation in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 (Shri Navaratnam is Asia-Pacific Managing Editor for Markets news at Dow Jones Newswires. He has 15 years of experience as a journalist and editor, having worked for news organizations in New Zealand, Singapore and Sri Lanka. He can be contacted on 65-64154-147 or by email: shri.navaratnam@dowjones)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAsia@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 24-09-10 0830GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1171 5008 70779   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100924e69o000jy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
