\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  up on stocks; won capped by govt\b0\par\par\uc2 998 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won up 0.3 pct on exporters, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted\par \par \uc2 * Peso up 0.3 pct on data; some see cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Yuan marginally lower, breaks six-days of rises\par \par \uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Malaysian ringgit and the South Korean won, rose on Friday helped by a rally in stocks globally and broad weakness in the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso found support from strong portfolio inflow data and demand from speculative funds, although some dealers suspected its rally was capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  were spotted buying dollars to cap the won's <KRW=> strength, feeding into market speculation that Asian policymakers are increasingly concerned about export competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 "Given strong Asian economic fundamentals and growing appetite for assets in the region, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to rise more. But I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities in the region will just let them rise, considering their exports," said Jeon Seung-ji, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Samsung Futures Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WON RISES\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> rose against the dollar on exporter demand before holidays next week and bids linked to foreign stock buying.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities bought dollars to prevent the won rising beyond 1,160 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed up 0.34 percent at 1,160.5 from Thursday's domestic close of 1,164.5 <KRW=KFTC>.\par \par \uc2 It rose as high as 1,159.2 during the day.\par \par \uc2 "The won is regaining a bullish trend, although the authorities will be a variable," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \par \uc2 The upside was also limited because dealers were wary of exposure to long won positions ahead of Korean holidays next week on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors bought a net 263.0 billion won in stocks, helping the benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> rise 0.86 percent.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The peso rose to 44.25 per dollar, up 0.3 percent, after data showed net portfolio inflows in August hit a 15-month high. [ID:nSGE68G00P]\par \par \uc2 But gains were checked by speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BSP) had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tap the rally on the head. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its presence to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rising too rapidly, a dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "There was talk of the BSP buying spot below 44.25 providing some support," said the dealer in Singapore. "Bids are expected to come at 44.15-20 again with the BSP supporting spot ahead of 44.00."\par \par \uc2 The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to rise further on a brighter outlook for the economy.\par \par \uc2 "Given strong growth expectation, we are pretty bullish on the peso. We think it will go to 44.00 per dollar at the end of this year," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in Singapore, asking not to be identified.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> rebounded in mid-afternoon trade to around 30.74 per dollar from 30.82 in the morning and 30.77 late on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "It is broadly in line with euro and Asian gains as the local concern over any capital controls by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fades. Finance Minister Korn's comments on encouraging offshore investment are an old story that should have very little to do with the baht's rebound this afternoon," a Bangkok-based trader said. [ID:nSGE68G06G]\par \par \uc2 The baht has risen 8.5 percent against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 YUAN\par \par \uc2 The yuan <CNY=CFXS> fell slightly against the dollar, breaking a straight six-session run of gains that pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 1 percent higher.\par \par \uc2 The rise marked the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's biggest six-day rally since January 2008 but dealers had become increasingly concerned about a pullback.\par \par \uc2 Still, traders said the yuan's uptrend would remain intact, arguing it could rise 2 percent or more in the coming three months. [ID:nTOE68E04U]\par \par \uc2 Traders said the latest yuan rally, engineered by the PBOC's setting of daily mid-points for trading, was a political move as U.S. pressure increases once more for Beijing to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise more quickly, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  generates the yuan's appreciation against the dollar this time purely to fend off political pressure instead of compensating for the yuan's loss against the basket," said a senior trader at a European bank in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 "Because such pressure will linger, even if it does not step up further, this leg of yuan rise could last for a few months, although there will still be ups and downs during the time." \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0630 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Curr