\par\par \b \uc2 S Korea Won Down Late On Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 2010\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     Close    Change \par  USD/KRW           1,184.1   +2.6 \par  JPY/KRW           13.4817   -0.1019 \par  3-Year Treasurys   3.86%    no change \par  5-Year Treasurys   4.41%    no change \par  10-Year Treasurys  4.87%    no change \par  20-Year Treasurys  5.06%    +1 bp \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won was lower late Wednesday on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in support of the dollar for a third day in a row.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities are suspected of having stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market early in the morning and again in late trade, buying dollars near KRW1,184 and KRW1,185, several traders said.\par \par \uc2 Two of those traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying to have been around $500 million to $1 billion.\par \par \uc2 "This seems to be an expression of (the authorities') determination not to allow a further slide in the dollar," which has fallen in the past six sessions, said a local bank trader.\par \par \uc2 Though most market participants expect the Bank of Korea to continue checking any further rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be able to only slow or interrupt the won's upward march given its positive fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's current-account surplus rose to a one-year high in June to $5.04 billion, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The downward trend still seems intact for the dollar, and there will be players waiting at higher levels to sell," for export settlements, or to take fresh dollar-short positions, said another local bank trader.\par \par \uc2 Domestic treasury bonds and bond futures ended nearly flat after a quiet session ahead of the release of the country's August treasury bond issue plan Thursday.\par \par \uc2 September bond futures ended one tick lower.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors snapped a nine-session buying streak in futures, selling a net 2,408 contracts, but the negative impact was minimal as the selling wasn't that aggressive.\par \par \uc2 "Players seem to be inclined to take this opportunity to cover their short positions in futures, against the foreign selling," said a trader at another local securities firm.\par \par \uc2 Amid conflicting views about the pace of the economic recovery in the second half, bond prices are largely dependent on the market's supply and demand conditions, which remain favorable amid ample liquidity in the system, participants said.\par \par \uc2 Some are even concerned that a bout of short covering could kick in and boost bonds, as many domestic investors are biased toward going short following the BOK's surprise rate hike earlier this month, said a bond manager at a local securities firm.\par \par \uc2 -By Min Jeong Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-3700-1900; min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com [ 28-07-10 0801GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1063 1858   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100728e67s000vs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
