\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA: Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  To Gain Gradually As Yuan Peg Ends\b0\par\par\uc2 By Arran Scott  \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires Column  \par \uc2 780 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2010\par 09:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged Monday as China's decision to drop the yuan's peg to the dollar revived expectations of a regional rally.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Indonesia and Thailand \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but strategists said Asia's authorities will likely tolerate a gradual appreciation after Beijing said Saturday it will let the yuan move more freely.\par \par \uc2 Gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as central banks tighten monetary policy, will likely be slow and in some cases fitful. Concerns about Europe's sovereign debt-crisis may continue to sap risk appetite, complicating the Asia rally.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  drove home the message that it will allow only gradual moves in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , setting the yuan's central parity rate at 6.8275 to the dollar, the same as Friday's fixing--and a weaker yuan level than the dollar's over-the-counter close Friday at CNY6.8262.\par \par \uc2 This was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  evidence of its policy of allowing more flexibility in the yuan exchange rate. Beijing had essentially pegged the dollar around CNY6.8300 since July 2008 as an emergency measure to combat the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 "It seems they're trying to avoid being seen as very aggressive," said Frances Cheung, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole Corporate and Investment Bank\uc2 . She forecasts the yuan will rise 1.5% against the dollar by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Investors, after the surprise fixing Monday morning knocked Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from early highs, nonetheless resumed buying yuan and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar dropped to CNY6.8015, its lowest under China's modern exchange-rate system, before rebounding somewhat. At 0650 GMT it was quoted at CNY6.8090.\par \par \uc2 "At the beginning the market was trying out around the level of Friday's close, but it has since turned to focus on the prospect of yuan appreciation in the near term," said a Shanghai trader at a foreign bank. "Everyone is selling dollars now."\par \par \uc2 Other Asian authorities are looking to China for cues. As the region's biggest export market with a rapidly growing economy, China is hugely important for other countries in Asia, and each government will likely try to ensure its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't deviate too much from those of its rival exporters.\par \par \uc2 Spencer Lin, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department at Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Taipei will pay attention to movements in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shift.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Deputy Gov. Hartadi Sarwono said, "The rupiah will adjust, as China's new policy will help trigger global economic recovery." Yet, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper the rise in the rupiah, which had jumped to its highest level since May 10. The dollar was at IDR9,065 at 0705 GMT, off its early low of IDR9,030.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea, warning against "one-sided" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, bought an estimated $1 billion for won, boosting the greenback to KRW1,172 from KRW1,169, Seoul traders said. The dollar remained well below late Friday's KRW1,202.6.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  was suspected to have bought a few hundred million dollars to slow the rise in the baht, which is up 3.1% against the dollar year-to-date.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may remain under gentle upward pressure. \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  expects a roughly 5% yuan rise by the middle of 2011, forecasting the dollar will fall to around CNY6.5000.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered says one way to play a yuan rise is through the New Taiwan dollar, which should benefit from the yuan de-pegging, given cross-strait trade links. The bank recommends selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via three-month nondeliverable forwards at an outright entry of TWD31.550, targeting a decline to TWD31.000.\par \par \uc2 "In our view, the Taiwan dollar is likely to catch up with other Asia ex-Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to become more tolerant of gradual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation," the bank said.\par \par \uc2 ING Bank is most bullish on the won, Taiwan dollar, Singapore dollar and Malaysian ringgit, "based on cheapness on real effective exchange-rate grounds and our assessment of central banks' tolerance for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation," said economist Tim Condon.\par \par \uc2 -By Arran Scott, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4042; arran.scott@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Shen Hong and Joy Shaw in Shanghai, Alex Pevzner in Taipei, Min-Jeong Lee in Seoul and Joko Hariyanto in Jakarta contributed to this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 21, 2010 03:28 ET (07:28 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100621e66l001bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
