\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  Won Down On Suspected BOK  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Up\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2010\par 09:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     Close    Change \par  USD/KRW           1,202.50  +7.60 \par  JPY/KRW            13.1421  +0.0473 \par  3-Year Treasurys   3.58%    -3 bps \par  5-Year Treasurys   4.36%    -3 bps \par  10-Year Treasurys  4.93%    -1 bp \par  20-Year Treasurys  5.20%    -1 bp \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--The South Korean won was lower late Monday largely due to suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in support of the dollar in late trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rebounding on active export settlements, several traders said.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities are suspected of having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently in recent months to curb any sharp gains in the won amid concerns that undue strength in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may sap an export-led recovery. But the latest move comes as a bit of a surprise as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen 7.8% in May--in the wake of the euro-zone debt crisis--its biggest monthly loss since February 2009.\par \par \uc2 Two traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have purchased between $300 million and $500 million, possibly via two foreign banks. "They (the authorities) may be wanting the dollar to flirt a while longer with levels above KRW1,200," before the won resumes its uptrend on a solid local economic recovery, said a foreign bank trader.\par \par \uc2 The dollar opened the domestic session sharply higher at KRW1,224 following news late last week that Fitch downgraded its credit ratings on Spain. But it quickly trimmed those gains to a low of KRW1,195 on active month-end export settlements before bouncing back up to KRW1,202.5 on the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Domestic treasury bonds and bond futures were moderately higher on weaker-than-expected industrial output data.\par \par \uc2 June bond futures gained nine ticks.\par \par \uc2 Official data released before the market open showed output in April rising 0.2% on a seasonally adjusted basis from the previous month, falling short of economists' expectation for a gain of 0.5%. Output was up a revised 1.7% in March.\par \par \uc2 The output data "will give more credence to the view that the local economic recovery momentum is slowing, leading treasury yields to continue heading to fresh lows for the year," said \uc2 Daishin Securities\uc2  fixed income analyst Jeong Im-bo.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark five-year yield had ended at a 2010 low of 4.26% on April 29.\par \par \uc2 Inflation data due Tuesday morning local time will come under intense scrutiny. The consumer price index likely rose 0.1% from a month earlier in May, according to the median forecast of 11 economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires. That would be a slowdown from April's 0.5% increase.\par \par \uc2 -By Min-Jeong Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-3700-1908; min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com [ 31-05-10 0746GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1063 1858   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100531e65v000i6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
