l Securities. Property developer \uc2 China Vanke\uc2  (000002.SZ) down 3.8% at CNY7.41, Poly Real Estate (600048.SH) down 4.7% at CNY11.58. Shenzhen Composite Index last down 1.5% at 1035.64. (rose.yu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0553 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR again starts falling on growing concerns that euro-zone's sovereign debt turmoil has started to undermine health of region's financial system, may extend declines to 1.2000 vs USD, 105.00 vs JPY in near term, says Masanobu Ishikawa, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Ueda Harlow. Notes many players have become worried over whether euro-zone's faltering financial system could drag down real economy in area; "it's extremely difficult to expect when the euro will hit bottom. Players remain very eager to sell the euro as economic conditions in Europe may worsen down the road." EUR/USD now at 1.2285 vs session high of 1.2372; EUR/JPY at 110.45 vs 111.62. Some traders say Europe investors just entering market, starting to sell EUR. (tomoyuki.tachikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0552 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW off 1,277.0 high on another round of suspected USD selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to 3-Seoul based traders; but pair still trading higher at 1,259.0 vs 1,214.5 late yesterday in Seoul on concerns over tensions between North, South Korea. "It's a crazy market that (I) haven't seen in a while," says local bank trader. Adds, pair still biased upward despite "the aggressive (dollar) selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." Traders decline to provide near term USD/KRW. Pair has traded in wide 1,224-1,277 range so far today. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0543 GMT 0000 GMT (Dow Jones) The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's decision to decline to offer Swiss franc repos in recent days suggests it is unwilling to accept lower franc money market rates, says \uc2 UBS\uc2 . "We attribute the latest decline in franc interest rates and negative rates on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  forward market to the excess liquidity in the local money market rather than anything else," says economist Reto Huenerwadel. "It's a fact, however, that over the last days the monetary conditions in Switzerland continued to loosen," he adds. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com) [ 05-25-10 0230ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100525e65p0004q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
