\par\par \b \uc2 S Korea Won Unchanged Late, Demand Offsets Impact From Greece Woes\b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2010\par 09:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     Close    Change \par  USD/KRW          1,108.70   +0.40 \par  JPY/KRW           11.8679   -0.0647 \par  3-Year Treasurys   3.76%    -1 bp \par  5-Year Treasurys   4.41%    -4 bps \par  10-Year Treasurys  4.91%    -3 bps \par  20-Year Treasurys  5.14%    -4 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--The South Korean won was nearly unchanged late Friday as strong demand for the local unit helped offset the renewed concerns over debt-ridden Greece.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Given the country's relatively solid economic fundamentals, the trend for next few weeks will be of a further appreciation in the won, except when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the gains, traders said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's growth likely accelerated in the first quarter from the previous three months as consumption improved, economists said. GDP likely grew a seasonally adjusted 1.5% in the first quarter. In the fourth quarter of 2009, GDP grew 0.2% on-quarter.\par \par \uc2 "Exporters and offshore hedge funds are still waiting for any rallies in the dollar to dump their dollar holdings," said a foreign bank trader.\par \par \uc2 "After about, let's say, a month, exporters and other players are bound to realize how the current dollar levels had been attractive to sell their dollars," said a local bank trader. "I expect the dollar to be at least off by some 20 won from here."\par \par \uc2 The negative impact on the won of news that Moody's Investors Service downgraded Greece's ratings was minimal, even though the euro fell to an 11-month low against the dollar following the announcement.\par \par \uc2 "This Greece issue has been such a prolonged one that its (negative) impact on the Seoul \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has somewhat worn off," said Byeon Ji-young, an analyst at Woori Futures.\par \par \uc2 Domestic treasury bonds and bond futures rose marginally as trade remained quiet ahead of the nation's first-quarter gross domestic output data. June bond futures gained seven ticks.\par \par \uc2 Bond prices have neared their previous highs again, so those anticipating a range bound market should consider taking profits around current levels, said Kim Sang-hoon, a fixed income analyst at \uc2 Hana Daetoo Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "So long as foreign investors--betting on stronger won-denominated assets in general--don't turn away from local bonds and bond futures, excessive selling doesn't seem appropriate," Kim said.\par \par \uc2 -By Min-Jeong Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-3700-1908; min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com [ 23-04-10 0737GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1063 1858   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100423e64n000o4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
