\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 870 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2010\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN OPPOSES PRESSURING CHINA ON YUAN BEFORE G-20 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor on Thursday signaled their opposition to openly pressuring China to revalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan, seemingly distancing themselves from the U.S. and European positions ahead of key international meetings. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER KAN: NO DEBATE ON YUAN AT G-7 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Minister Naoto Kan said he and his G-7 counterparts and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heads spent most of their time discussing Greece's problems at a working dinner Thursday, largely leaving aside the issues of China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and reforms to the global financial system. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA GOVERNOR: OUTLOOK FOR MONETARY POLICY REMAINS "AN OPEN ONE" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian interest rates for borrowers and depositors are now "pretty close" to the average of the past 10 to 12 years, Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens said Friday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA SWAN: SHALLOW DOWNTURN MEANS RECOVERY FROM POSITION OF STRENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The shallow downturn in Australia means the economy is recovering from a position of strength relative to other developed nations, Treasurer Wayne Swan said at an investor briefing in New York Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE MINISTRY: 2010 RETAIL SALES TO GROW AROUND 16% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's retail sales are likely to grow around 16% this year, partly due to rising inflationary pressures amid the economy's recovery, the Ministry of Commerce said Friday. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN BANK MINISTER CALLS FOR LOOSE SUPERVISION AS GOLDMAN PROBE CONTINUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's banking minister Friday called for a hands-off approach to financial supervision in Japan, speaking even as authorities across the Pacific proceeded with their fraud probe against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI CAPITAL ON EDGE AFTER DEADLY GRENADE BLASTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand was on edge Friday after a series of grenade attacks in the heart of Bangkok that left three people dead and scores wounded in the latest bloodshed of the escalating political crisis. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN IMPORT PRICE INDEX +0.3% IN 1Q, EXPORT INDEX +3.8% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A price index of Australian imports rose 0.3% in the first quarter of 2010 from the fourth quarter 2009, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said Friday. (published 0132 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ MIGRANT INFLOWS REMAIN STRONG, HELP SUSTAIN GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Migrant inflows into New Zealand surged nearly three-fold in the twelve months ended March, helping sustain growth in the nation as new comers boost retail spending and housing services. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ'S MARCH CREDIT CARD BILLINGS +1.2% VS FEB, +6.3% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's total credit card billings rose in March from February, data issued Friday by the Reserve \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  showed. (published 0307 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA TO GIVE SMALLER BUILDERS KRW3 TLN FOR UNSOLD APARTMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will give KRW3 trillion to buy some 20,000 unsold apartments to help smaller builders fight a shortage of liquidity. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: VIETNAM APRIL CPI +9.23% ON YEAR, +0.14% ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's consumer price index in April rose 9.23% from a year earlier, led by higher transport, housing and building materials costs and prices of foodstuff, the General Statistics Office said Friday. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TITAN PETROCHEMICALS MAKES NEW OFFER TO EXCHANGE US DOLLAR BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil trader and shipper \f28 \uc2 \f2 Titan Petrochemicals Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it plans to make a new offer worth US$254.2 million in total, comprising U.S. dollar senior notes, convertible bonds and a cash payment, to buy back its outstanding US$315.4 million worth of U.S. dollar senior notes due 2012. (published 0034 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA COSCO HOLDINGS TO ISSUE UP TO CNY10B MEDIUM-TERM NOTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Cosco Holdings Co. said Thursday it plans to issue up to CNY10 billion in five-year notes to supplement liquidity and repay bank loans. (published 2342 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GLORIOUS PROPERTY NOT PROCEEDING WITH BOND OFFERING FOR NOW - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glorious Property Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is not proceeding with a bond offering after concluding a series of meetings with global bond investors, a person familiar with the company's plans said Friday. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: EURO/DOLLAR OPTIONS UP AS SPOT HITS 11-MONTH LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro/dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options gained in Asia Friday as the underlying exchange rate hit an 11-month low due to ongoing worries over Greece's debt problems. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: YEN TO RESUME FALL ON US-JAPAN RATE GAP; DOLLAR MAY HIT Y100 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen looks set to resume its fall, with the dollar possibly rising toward a one-year high of Y100, as investors once again focus on the widening gap between U.S. and Japanese interest rates. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SOUTH KOREA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TAKE BOLDER STEPS ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ? \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recent appointment of several key economic officials has players expecting a more forceful government presence in South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market--but a closer look at the country's fundamentals suggests their concerns may be misplaced. (published 0315 GMT) [ 23-04-10 0400GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100423e64n0008q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
