\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won hits 2-wk high,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  spotted\b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 02:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Won gains 0.5 pct to 2-week high\par \par \uc2  * Foreign investors buy local stocks for 13th session in row\par \par \uc2  * Dealers report dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2   (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, March 30 (Reuters) - The won rose half a percent to a near 2-week high against the dollar on Tuesday as the euro's rebound eased concerns about Europe's debt problems and as foreign stock funds kept rushing into \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Dealers reported South Korean authorities buying dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at stemming the won's <KRW=> <KRW=KFTC> fast appreciation, which policymakers in the country are worried would hurt the competitiveness of its exporters.\par \par \uc2  Dealers said the won was supported by growing risk preference, but demand for dollars remained solid from importers and foreign shareholders in local companies, who recently received dividend payouts for the last year.\par \par \uc2  "Offshore players have been leading bids for the won since yesterday but I think the won's upside will be limited at around 1,128 (per dollar)," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \par \uc2  The won ended the session at 1,130.1 per dollar after rising to as high as 1,129.6, its strongest since March 18, compared with Monday's domestic close of 1,135.5.\par \par \uc2  Foreign investors extended their net buying spree on Seoul's main stock exchange to a 13th consecutive session, setting the longest successive buying streak since September last year.\par \par \uc2  The exchange's benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> ended up 0.5 percent at 1,700.19 points, its strongest finish since Jan. 21, as foreign investors bought a net 258 billion won ($228 million) worth of local shares.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  added to the bullish mood by upgrading its 3-month view on the won to 1,100 from 1,150 previously, citing prospects for an improving international balance of payments and an interest rate increase later this year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data also showed on Tuesday that South Korean manufacturing firms, relying heavily on exports, were the most optimistic in at least seven years about their business conditions in the coming month. [ID:nSUL000014]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par               0600 GMT      0030 GMT    prev close\par  Won           1,130.1   1,131.2/1.7       1,135.5\par  Yen/won   12.2175/287   12.2666/786   12.2491/580\par  KOSPI        1,700.19      1,701.46      1,691.99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Reporting by Yoo Choonsik; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100402e63u0000v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
