\par\par \b \uc2 INDIAN MORNING BRIEFING: Sensex Could Rally To 16,530\b0\par\par\uc2 1,873 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2010\par 04:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL MARKETS \par DJIA           10185.53  +118.20  +1.17% \par Nasdaq          2171.20  +23.65   +1.11% \par S&P 500         1089.19  +15.32   +1.43% \par FTSE 100        5247.41  +58.89   +1.14% \par Nikkei Stock   10381.51  +176.49  +1.73% \par Hang Seng      20486.00  +242.25  +1.20% \par Kospi           1615.61  +9.17    +0.57% \par SGX Nifty       4945.50  +44.50   +0.91% \par Feb contract \par  \par USD/JPY       90.65-68     +0.89% \par Range         90.94-89.81 \par EUR/USD       1.3926-27    +0.45% \par Range         1.3935-1.3854 \par  \par CBOT Wheat March    $4.746 per bushel \par Comex Gold          $1105.00  +$21.20 \par Comex Gold Range    $1077.20-$1107.90 \par Nymex Crude (NY)    $74.43     +$1.54 \par  \par  \par CHARTING THE SENSEX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bombay Stock Exchange's 30-share index could rally to 16,530, according to charts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 After a weak opening Monday, the index staged a sharp recovery later in the session. This is a positive sign. A move past the immediate resistance at 16,530 would impart momentum to the uptrend and the index could then rally to 16,850.\par \par \uc2 But the short-term bullish view would be negated if the index falls below Friday's intra-day low of 15,980.\par \par \uc2 The National Stock Exchange's 50-share NSE Nifty could rally to 4,930, according to charts.\par \par \uc2 A move past this immediate resistance would be a sign of strength and could trigger a rally to 4,970.\par \par \uc2 The short-term bullish outlook would be invalidated on a close below 4,825. A fall below this would suggest that the index is headed to major support at 4,540.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks rose broadly Monday as better-than-expected quarterly earnings from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Exxon Mobil\f28 \uc2 \f2  and a rebound in crude oil prices lifted the energy sector, while materials stocks including \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alcoa\f28 \uc2 \f2  and DuPont were boosted by a rise in metals futures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average climbed 1.17%, marking its first rise in three sessions and its biggest one-day gain since Jan. 4. The measure is still off 2.33% for the year to date, thanks to a rough losing spell in the latter part of January.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alcoa\f28 \uc2 \f2  and DuPont were the Dow's best performers, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Exxon Mobil\f28 \uc2 \f2  not far behind. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alcoa\f28 \uc2 \f2  jumped 5%, while DuPont rose 3.2%, as metals futures climbed, with gold futures snapping a three-session losing streak and silver and copper ending four-session losing streaks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exxon Mobil\f28 \uc2 \f2  climbed 2.7% after its fourth-quarter earnings beat expectations, though they were still down 23% as lower margins on refining and fuels and lower natural gas prices were partly offset by higher crude prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday's stock gains came as manufacturing data from the Institute for Supply Management came in above expectations, showing the U.S. factory sector booked its best performance in more than five years in January.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The excitement over the ISM report largely outweighed investors' concerns about President Barack Obama's budget plan, which would shrink the current deficit to $727 billion, or 4.2% of the gross domestic product, by 2013, but add $8.5 trillion to the federal debt through 2020, pushing the debt as a percentage of GDP to 77%, up from 53%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were higher Tuesday as gains in Wall Street buoyed sentiment, with auto makers in Japan rising after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  took steps to fix recalled vehicles.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Nikkei 225, Australia's S&P/ASX 200, South Korea's Kospi Composite and New Zealand's NZX-50 were all higher. Dow Jones Industrial Average futures were up 4 points in screen trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think we're in for a good day's trade, but you still have to consider the downside risks because it's a fickle market," said IG Markets Institutional Dealer Chris Weston in Sydney. "I think people want to see Wall Street prove itself."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Japan, auto makers were rising on short-covering. Toyota's shares were heavily sold recently after it recalled vehicles in the U.S. and Europe because some gas pedals were sticking.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota was up 4.3%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which also announced a worldwide recall of 646,000 compact cars to examine defective window switches, advanced 2.2%, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 2.8%. Shipping and oil plays were higher, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nippon Yusen\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 2.0%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsui O.S.K\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Lines up 2.5% and Inpex 2.0%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean shares were led higher by gains in steelmakers and technology names, mostly tracking their U.S. peers. "The U.S. markets' rebound overnight following recent falls improved sentiment, leading foreign investors to resume stock buying," said Lee Sun-yup at Shinhan Investment Corporation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  added 0.6% and LG Display rose 1.4%; among steelmakers, Posco was up 2.3%. However, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  gave up 2.6% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kia Motors\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 1.7% on profit-taking, despite data Monday showing strong January car sales.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar slipped from six-month highs Monday as evidence of a global economic recovery drove investors to higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Late Monday in New York, the euro was at $1.3930, up from $1.3866 late Friday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y90.65, up from Y90.29, while the euro was at Y126.29, up from Y125.22. The U.K. pound was at $1.5962, down from $1.6004.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold was bid at $1,105.60 per troy ounce, up $1.90 from the New York close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March Nymex crude oil futures were up 48 cents at $74.91 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CALENDAR OF EVENTS Feb. 2 \par N/A        Mumbai:     Securities and Exchange Board of India board meet \par 1045 IST   Bangalore:  India defense minister and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharat Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                        chairman at inauguration of new facility \par 1115 IST   New Delhi:  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Siemens AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  press briefing \par 1115 IST   New Delhi:  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mahanagar Telephone Nigam\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aksh Optifibre\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                        joint press conference \par 1300 IST   New Delhi:  German President Horst Kohler at joint FICCI- \par                        CII event \par 1430 IST   Mumbai:     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kotak Mahindra Old Mutual Life Insurance\f28 \uc2 \f2  2010 \par                        outlook \par 1500 IST   New Delhi:  India Prime Minister Manmohan Singh to address \par                        Mahatma Gandhi NREGA Sammelan 2010 \par 0930 GMT UK            January CIPS construction PMI \par 1000 GMT EU            December PPI \par N/A      US            January auto sales \par 1245 GMT US            January 30 ICSC/\f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  chain store sales \par 1355 GMT US            January 30 Redbook index \par 1500 GMT US            Treasury Secretary Geithner testifies in Washington \par 1500 GMT US            December pending home sales \par 2130 GMT US            January 29 API oil industry report \par 2200 GMT US            January 31 ABC/Washington Post consumer confidence index \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Dow Jones/WSJ \par CHINA: U.S. TRADE PROTECTIONISM RISING SINCE FINANCIAL CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. has been increasingly engaging in trade protectionism since the onset of the global financial crisis, which has seriously affected trade relations between the U.S. and China, China's Ministry of Commerce said Monday. (published 0022 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES RISE TO RECORD IN JANUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rebounded to an all-time high in January, propelled by investment gains, the retrieval of dollar loans and suspected dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SOUTH KOREA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO LIMIT GAINS FROM PUBLIC SERVICE CHARGES TO STABLILIZE PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government aims to maintain price stability by limiting any potential gains from public service charges, such as for electricity, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Tuesday. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF'S BLANCHARD:CENTRAL BANKS SHOULD LEAVE RATES VERY LOW-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central banks should keep interest rates very low, the International Monetary Fund's chief economist Olivier Blanchard says in an interview to appear in Tuesday's edition of French business daily Les Echos. (published 1849 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREEK PM: WILL DO 'EVERYTHING NECESSARY' TO END FISCAL CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greek Prime Minister George Papandreou pledged Monday to do "everything necessary" to pull the country out of a fiscal hole that has hurt its standing on the financial markets. (published 2024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ARROW ENERGY CONFIRMS IT'S MULLING FUNDING OPTIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Arrow Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it is considering a number of options to fund the proposed liquefied natural gas terminal at Fisherman's Landing in Queensland state, including sourcing more debt, issuing new shares, or selling down part of its interest in the project. (published 0026 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIO TINTO COMPLETES SALES OF ALCAN PACKAGING TO AMCOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has completed the US$1.948 billion sale of its Alcan packaging assets to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amcor Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the two companies said in statements Tuesday. (published 2227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 HILLS INDUSTRIES\f28 \uc2 \f2  IMPRESSES WITH 40% 1H PROFIT BOOST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Home and hardware products maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hills Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Tuesday upgraded its full year earnings guidance after it surprised the market with a better-than-expected 40% rise in first half profit. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIAN AIR CEO: 2010 WILL BE BETTER YEAR THAN 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian Airline System Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects 2010 to be a better year than 2009 but still sees competitive challenges ahead, the firm's chief executive said. (published 0039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: JPMORGAN BALKS ON RBS SEMPRA NORTH AMERICAN OPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is reconsidering its interest in acquiring the North American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of RBS \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sempra Commodities\f28 \uc2 \f2  but remains in talks to buy the firm's European metals and energy trading \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , people familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par METLIFE TO CONSOLIDATE 2 CHINA INSURANCE JV \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 China's insurance regulator has approved Capital Airports Holding Co. to sell its 50% stake in a life-insurance joint venture with \f28 \uc2 \f2 MetLife Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to Shanghai Alliance Investment Ltd., said the U.S. life insurer, paving the way for \f28 \uc2 \f2 MetLife\f28 \uc2 \f2  to consolidate its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in China. (published 0146 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOEING EXEC: ON TRACK TO DELIVER 787 TO ANA BY END-2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-02-10 0302GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boeing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is on track to deliver the first 787 Dreamliner aircraft to Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 All Nippon Airways Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by the end of this year, a senior official said Tuesday. (published 0137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA ERZHONG HEAVY INDUSTRIES OPENS AT CNY8.50 VS IPO CNY8.50 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Erzhong Group Heavy Industries Co. opened flat at CNY8.50 on its debut on the Shanghai Stock Exchange Tuesday, above analysts' expectations. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Indian Media \par Indian Government Set To Sell 10%-15% \f28 \uc2 \f2 Coal India\f28 \uc2 \f2  Stake In Next 6 Months - PTI \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hinduja Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Close To Acquisition Of Indian Construction Company - PTI \par Renault To Set Up Own Dealership In India - Economic Times \par Genpact In Talks For Possible Acquisition Of Intelenet Global Services - Economic Times \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 JSW Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  To Invest Over INR500 Bln In Power Projects Over 5 Years - PTI \par Hindalco Industries To Make Beverage Cans In India - Business Standard \par Fire At SAIL's Bhilai Steel Pla