\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  Won Higher Late; Bank Of Korea Likely  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  Again\b0\par\par\uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2009\par 09:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     Close    Change \par  USD/KRW           1,164.50  -6.70 \par  JPY/KRW            12.6466  -0.1255 \par  3-Year Treasuries  4.41%    +2 bps \par  5-Year Treasuries  4.92%    +2 bps \par  10-Year Treasuries 5.39%    -1 bp \par  20-Year Treasuries 5.61%    unchanged \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--The South Korean won was higher late Wednesday on active dollar-selling by local exporters, but its gains were again capped by suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market toward the end of the session to cap a rise in the won, four Seoul-based traders said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely bought the dollar around KRW1,163, largely via a state-run bank, they said. One of those traders at a local bank estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have bought between $300 million and $500 million.\par \par \uc2 Market participants observed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stepping into the market frequently in recent months to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, which has gained around 35% since its low in March. Domestic authorities are concerned that the won's persistent strength may sap an export-led recovery in Asia's fourth largest economy.\par \par \uc2 A foreign bank trader said that the greenback is poised for more falls next year.\par \par \uc2 "With the continued current account surpluses, (the dollar's) supply still outweighs demand. And we will see more selling from heavy industry firms next year," said the trader. "The appropriate direction for the dollar/won is for it to go downwards," which will likely prompt further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the domestic authorities.\par \par \uc2 After a listless session in the morning, the dollar hit an intraday low of KRW1,162.60 in the afternoon as exporters started selling aggressively due to their year-end settlements while offshore investors also sold greenbacks.\par \par \uc2 The won was up 0.6% for the day, 8.2% for this year.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday was the last trading day for the local spot market for the year. Trading will resume Monday, when the market will open at 0100 GMT, an hour later than its usual opening time.\par \par \uc2 Domestic treasury bonds ended mixed after a listless session. March bond futures lost six ticks as foreigners were net sellers of bond futures for a sixth straight session.\par \par \uc2 Bonds largely brushed off government data issued earlier in day that showed South Korea's industrial production increased 17.8% in November from a year earlier, accelerating from 0.2% growth in October.\par \par \uc2 "The numbers are good, but the data aren't much of a surprise," as the market had expected some 17% growth, said a bond manager at a local asset management firm.\par \par \uc2 Bargain hunting may provide support for bonds next week after some steep falls since early December. But any strong rebound from current levels seems unlikely as investors aren't anticipating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor to make dovish comments at the upcoming Bank of Korea's meeting in January, he added.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the regular local bond market will be closed while the over-the-counter bond market will open as usual. Both markets will be closed Friday and resume trading Monday.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark five-year yield has gained 115 basis points so far this year.\par \par \uc2 -By Min-Jeong Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-3700-1908; min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com [ 30-12-09 0815GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1063 1858   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091230e5cu000cf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
