\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  Won Tad Up Late,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Concerns Cap Gains\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2009\par 08:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    Close    Change \par USD/KRW           1,154.10  -0.70 \par JPY/KRW            12.9543  +0.0587 \par 3-Year Treasuries  4.24%    -5 bps \par 5-Year Treasuries  4.82%    -8 bps \par 10-Year Treasuries 5.40%    -6 bps \par 20-Year Treasuries 5.56%    -3 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--The South Korea won was a touch higher late Tuesday, paring gains on corporate demand for the greenback and concerns the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  climb too fast.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The won had opened stronger against the dollar, reflecting rising risk appetite following gains in U.S. stocks overnight, but companies buying the greenback on dips helped to cushion the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Among those fuelling demand was state-run \uc2 Korea Electric Power Corp\uc2 . (015760.SE), which entered the Seoul \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second straight day, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 The person said the purchases were made so the company could repay its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated debt, but declined to comment on the amount that Kepco bought on either day.\par \par \uc2 Kepco, which has a total of $1.25 billion of euro- and yen-denominated offshore debt falling due next week, plans to buy more than $1.2 billion in Seoul's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this week, the person said.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar demand (from Kepco) seems have been quite significant today," said a local bank trader.\par \par \uc2 After rebounding from an intraday low of KRW1,149.70 hit after the market just opened, the dollar ended the session at its weakest since Sept. 23, 2008, when it sank to KRW1,149.00.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar remains bearish. But for the dollar-won to make a convincing break below the 1,150 level, the euro would have to continue trading comfortably above the key $1.5000 resistance," said a foreign bank trader.\par \par \uc2 The euro--a general barometer of risk appetite--was trading lower at $1.4955 in late Asian trade, compared with $1.5005 in New York Monday.\par \par \uc2 Domestic treasury bonds and bond futures rose sharply after monetary authorities both in the U.S. and domestically further bolstered perceptions that interest rates will stay extremely low for an extended period of time, with December bond futures gaining 24 ticks.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Korea Senior Deputy Governor Kim Jae-chun said in a statement prepared for a global financial conference in Seoul: "If we raise the policy rate hastily, it'll hurt the recovery of the Korean economy," though Kim added that "keeping the rate low for too long will also impair the long-term growth potential."\par \par \uc2 Overnight, U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke sounded a cautious note on the U.S. economy, prompting investors to stock up on U.S. Treasurys.\par \par \uc2 "The buying interest spread to the longer tenor bonds today," which had been underperforming the shorter ones recently, said a bond manager at an asset management firm.\par \par \uc2 "Bonds might correct some gains on the way, but the overall bullish sentiment will likely persist" until the release of economic data at the end of the month, he added.\par \par \uc2 -By Min-Jeong Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-2198-2230; min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com [ 17-11-09 0757GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1063 1858   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091117e5bh000jk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
