\par\par \b \uc2 HIGHLIGHTS-South Korean  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief's comments\b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2009\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For full coverage, double-click [ID:nSP479672])\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The Bank of Korea's chief prompted investors on Friday to scale back their bets on a rate rise this year, noting signs of cooling in the property market and predicting economic growth would taper off this quarter.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its key interest rate steady at a record low of 2.0 percent on Friday for the eighth month in a row as expected, saying uncertainty over the global demand remained and the domestic inflation was stable.\par \par \uc2 Following are a selection of Bank of Korea Governor Lee Seong-tae's remarks at a news conference, translated by Reuters:\par \par \uc2 ON PROPERTY MARKET\par \par \uc2 "The real estate market shows signs of moderating since mid-September. Stabilising property market should reduce the burden on monetary authorities...But it's too soon to say the property market has fully stabilised. We need to watch more whether property prices will stabilise further or revive after a break."\par \par \uc2 "The government has taken several regulatory steps, which seem to be working in bringing down the pace of mortgage lending growth...And the recent rise in borrowing rates appears to have had some effect, as well, I believe."\par \par \uc2 ON INTEREST RATES, EXIT STRATEGY\par \par \uc2 "Current policy rate represents a considerable monetary easing, when taking into account our economic growth pace, inflation and market rates. The rate is also low when taking into account the mid- to long-term economic prospects."\par \par \uc2 "We don't decide rates only based on the property market situation. It's true that the property issue has been a major concern for us since the second quarter. (But) the most important determinants are consumer prices and economy."\par \par \uc2 "In September I wanted to send signals that rate hikes were not far away and could come earlier than expected, and it seems that some people took the comments as indicating an imminent rate change."\par \par \uc2 "Australia raised its rate to 3.25 percent from 3.0 percent but that cannot be viewed as an exit strategy."\par \par \uc2 "Market rates have risen but they are not yet so high as to give big troubles to households or companies."\par \par \uc2 "I understand the global coordination in exit policy as a call for countries to consider its influence, positive or negative, on the global economy as well as on the other nations when setting a policy."\par \par \uc2 ON ECONOMY, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 "Global economic conditions, which are a major factor for our economy, are improving gradually since the start of the second half but I'm not confident of a strong recovery yet. There remain many uncertainties over the global economic growth."\par \par \uc2 "Our economy continues its recovery. The third-quarter GDP growth is likely to be better than expected. But the fourth-quarter growth is not seen as strong as in the second and third quarters."\par \par \uc2 "Inflation will likely stabilise in 2009 and 2010 from high levels seen in 2007 and 2008. The domestic inflation is expected to hover around our target of 3 percent level."\par \par \uc2 ON \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 , CURRENT ACCOUNT\par \par \uc2 "As a small open economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to carry out some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 "The won's tumbling to 1,500 to the dollar in the wake of the global financial crisis was an over-reaction, given our economic strength. The recent rise is understood as a correction to that."\par \par \uc2 "It's hard to say what is the proper level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. But a sharp fluctuation is a concern."\par \par \uc2 "The current account surplus for this year can be far bigger than initially expected. The surplus will decline next year but not to a worrisome extent." (Reporting by Seo Eun-kyung; Editing by Yoo Choonsik)\par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/RATES (HIGHLIGHTS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091009e5a9000dj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
