\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 8\b0\par\par\uc2 1,631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2009\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: ASIA CENTRAL BANKS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AGAIN AS DOLLAR TUMBLES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar continued to tumble against most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday, prompting another wave of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by central banks in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Taiwan, and the Philippines seeking to limit damage to their export industries. (published 0343 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA JOBS SURGE BOOSTS RBA HIKE EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of employed Australians surged in September, defying economists' expectations of a fall and firming up expectations of more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  interest rate increases this year. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:JAPAN AUG CURR ACCT SURPLUS UP,BUT LOW RATES DRAG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's current account surplus rose slightly less than expected in August, as low interest rates overseas and the strong yen ate into Japanese firms' investment earnings, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOK MAY HAVE BOUGHT AROUND $500MLN-$1BLN IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MKT - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea may have bought between $500 million and $1 billion in the spot market earlier Thursday to cap the won's rise, traders said. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:THAI CTRL BK ADMITS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS BAHT RISE TOO FAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday that it has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market recently because the baht has been too strong against its fundamentals since early this month. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA WPI UP 0.70% ON YEAR IN WEEK ENDED SEP 26 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's inflation rate eased to 0.70% in the week ended Sept. 26 from 0.83% in the previous week, the Ministry of Commerce and Industry said Thursday. (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: WILL STICK TO EXPANSIONARY FISCAL POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will stick to its expansionary fiscal policy for the time being as private sector activity continues to be tepid and the strength of the global economy's recovery remains uncertain, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday. (published 0115 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT:TO LIMIT STATE-RUN COS FROM SEEKING FUNDS OVERSEAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will limit state-run firms from seeking dollar-funding overseas in a bid to slow the won's rise against the greenback, a senior official at the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA FINCL WATCHDOG TIGHTENS NON-BK SECTOR HOME MTGE RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Financial Supervisory Service said Thursday it is tightening the risk management of housing mortgage loans extended by non-bank financial institutions amid a sharp rise in such lending. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN BANKS TO RAISE RATES AFTER RBA MOVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's major lenders on Thursday said they will increase interest rates on home loans and deposits in response to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's surprise increase to its official cash rate on Tuesday. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGTEL OPTUS LOOKING TO SELL 10-YR BENCHMARK USD BOND-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singtel Optus Pty Ltd. is looking to sell a 10-year benchmark U.S. dollar bond and aims to price the debt this week, a person familiar with the deal said Thursday. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: LUMENA RESOURCES TO SELL MAIDEN GLOBAL US DOLLAR BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese minerals company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lumena Resources Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it is looking to sell its first-ever global U.S. dollar bond to repay debt and finance its expansion. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI SEPTEMBER CONSUMER CONFIDENCE INDEX 75.6 VS 74.5 AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer confidence in Thailand improved in September for a fourth straight month, due mainly to lower oil prices and the government's economic stimulus package. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LARSEN EXEC:RAISED $600M VIA SALE OF SHARES, CONV DEBENTURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Larsen & Toubro Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has raised $600 million by selling shares and convertible debentures, a spokesman said Thursday. (published 0421 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ANTAM: MAY BUY STAKE IN BHP'S INDONESIAN COAL ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned nickel and gold mining company \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Aneka Tambang\f28 \uc2 \f2  is considering acquiring a stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Indonesian coal assets as part of its plan to buy a coal project as early as this year, an executive at Antam, as the company is known, said Thursday. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: WESTPAC LOSES NZ COURT TAX CASE, MUST PAY NZ$961M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Westpac Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost a New Zealand High Court case against the Inland Revenue Department and now owes NZ$961 million in taxes and interest, the government department said Thursday. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LAWSON 1H GRP NET PFT Y16.03B VS Y15.51B PFT YR EARLIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Convenience store operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lawson Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its revenue and profit for the first half ended August grew on year, due to strength at its discount store unit as well as in sales of its reasonably priced own-brand products. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FAMILYMART 1H GRP NET PFT Y9.86B VS Y11.75B PFT YR EARLIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Convenience store operator FamilyMart Co. said Thursday its net profit for the fiscal first half through August dropped 16% as weak consumer demand and poor summer weather dented its sales. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE SIGMA PHARMA RETAIL OFFER ONLY 32% SUBSCRIBED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sigma Pharmaceuticals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., an Australian drug maker, said Thursday that its retail share entitlement offer was only 32% subscribed. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TRANSFIELD SERVICES RENEWS 5-YR AGREEMENT IN US WITH CHEVRON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian engineering and asset management firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Transfield Services\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday it renewed its contract to provide maintenance services at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chevron Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . oil refineries in the U.S. for another five years. (published 2251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BAOSTEEL ASKED TO RESUBMIT AQUILA FIRB APPLICATION - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Baosteel Group Corp. has been asked by Australia's Foreign Investment Review Board, or FIRB, to resubmit its application to take a 15% stake in junior coal and iron ore group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aquila Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 2226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CAPITALAND TO HOLD EGM OCT 30 FOR VOTE ON LISTING OF MALL OPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Southeast Asia's largest property developer by assets, \f28 \uc2 \f2 CapitaLand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., Thursday said that it will call for an extraordinary general meeting to vote on its plan to list its Asia-wide retail properties in Singapore. (published 2318 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par METRO PACIFIC RAISES PHP1.86B MORE FROM PRIVATE PLACEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Metro Pacific Investments Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it has raised an additional PHP1.86 billion, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 CLSA Singapore Pte Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . exercised its option to buy more shares offered in a private placement. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI BOURSE HALTS TRADE IN THAINOX PENDING STAKE DEAL INFO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Stock Exchange of Thailand has halted trading in shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thainox Stainless PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  from Thursday morning after speculation that its major shareholders are looking to sell their stake to a new alliance. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIABULLS POWER SETS IPO PRICE BAND AT INR40-INR45 A SHARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's Indiabulls Power Ltd. said Thursday it has set the price band for its initial public offering at INR40-INR45 a share. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: SPOT GOLD HITS RECORD, USD WEAK ON RISK APPETITE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold hit a new record high in Asia Thursday, breaking above resistance at $1,050 a troy ounce with traders predicting a "blue skies scenario," led by a resurgence in dollar weakness. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BHP BILLITON TIGHT LIPPED ON OLYMPIC DAM ACCIDENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it will take two weeks to assess the impact of a mechanical failure at its Olympic Dam mine on copper, gold and uranium production from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in South Australia state. (published 0448 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: SHELL PLANS US$5B FLOATING LNG OFF W AUSTRALIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday it has commenced site-specific design work for what could be the world's first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  floating liquefied natural gas platform. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ANTAM: MAY BUY STAKE IN BHP'S INDONESIAN COAL ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned nickel and gold mining company \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Aneka Tambang\f28 \uc2 \f2  is considering acquiring a stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Indonesian coal assets as part of its plan to buy a coal project as early as this year, an executive at Antam, as the company is known, said Thursday. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE 2010 RICE IMPORTS MAY HOVER NEAR 2M TONS -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine rice imports next year could hover near the 2 million metric ton mark following extensive damage to rice crops wrought by two powerful typhoons, a senior agriculture official said Thursday. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:THAI RUBBER SUPPLIES LOWER THAN NORMAL ON HEAVY RAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's rubber output is likely to be dragged down due to rains in the country's south during the October-December quarter, a senior industry executive said Thursday. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SHELL IN DISCUSSIONS ON GLADSTONE LNG CONSOLIDATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Executive Director, Upstream International, Malcolm Brinded said Thursday the company is in consolidation talks with other ventures planning to build liquefied natural gas plants at Gladstone in Queensland state. (published 0436 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA'S PETRONAS: TO WORK WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 GAZPROM\f28 \uc2 \f2  ON U.K. GAS VENTURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's state-owned oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroliam Nasional Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petronas\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Thursday that its U.K. unit Petgas Trading Ltd. has entered into a number of collaborative ventures with a unit of Russian gas producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 OAO Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: DINGXIN, BINTANG DELAPAN TO BUILD NICKEL SMELTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-10-09 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Dingxin Group and Indonesia's Bintang Delapan Group will invest up to $1 billion over the next five years to develop a nickel smelting facility in Central Sulawesi province, Bintang Delapan President Director Halim Mina said Wednesday. (published 0129 GMT) [ 08-10-09 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091008e5a8000cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
