\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 6\b0\par\par\uc2 1,519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2009\par 09:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =3RD UPDATE: RBA FIRST G-20 CTRL BANK TO START TIGHTENING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Tuesday raised interest rates for the first time since March 2008, becoming the first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Group of 20 to begin withdrawing stimulus that has sustained the economy through the global financial crisis. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =ASIAN AUTHORITIES STEP UP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS DOLLAR SLIDES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central banks in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Singapore and Thailand likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday to curb the rise of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , reflecting an effort by many Asian countries to keep their exporters competitive as the U.S. dollar swoons. (published 0655 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN DEPUTY PM KAN: MAY NEED TO MAKE FY09 2ND EXTRA BUDGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Deputy Prime Minister Naoto Kan said Tuesday he personally thinks the government may need to compile a second extra budget for the current fiscal year ending March to prepare for any contingency. (published 0327 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN HIRANO:TO MULL JGB ISSUANCE AFTER ASSESSING TAX REVENUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary Hirofumi Hirano said Tuesday the government will decide whether to issue new bonds in the fiscal year starting April 2010 after carefully assessing tax revenues. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:FUJII:HOPE BOJ ACTS CAUTIOUSLY ON CORP FUND OPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii said Tuesday that he hasn't heard that the Bank of Japan will decide this month on whether to scrap some of its emergency funding measures, but said he hopes the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will carefully monitor the economy before making such a decision. (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA AUG TRADE GAP NARROWS BUT EXPORTS STRUGGLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's trade gap narrowed in August from July but was much wider than expected as the value of exports failed to improve due to falls in coal exports and a stronger Australian dollar. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ 3Q BUSINESS CONFIDENCE SURGES TO DECADE HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's business confidence leapt to a decade high in the third quarter, reinforcing evidence that the economy is pulling out of a recession that began in early 2008. (published 2322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:PHILIPPINE SEP CPI +0.7% ON YR;INFLATION MAY ACCELERATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines accelerated in September, driven by increases in food prices and dissipating effects of a higher price base last year, and may pick up pace in the coming months due to the impact of recent typhoons and increased demand during the holiday season. (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA SWAN SAYS POLICY STIMULUS SUPPORTING ECON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Treasurer Wayne Swan said Tuesday both fiscal and monetary policy is continuing to support economic growth, and an unwinding of both would stifle a recovery. (published 0446 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:KOREA SEP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES SURGE,MAY RISE MORE BY YR-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves rose for a seventh straight period in September to the highest in 15 months, and may surge to a record by year-end with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely stepping up purchases of the dollar to stem an increase in the value of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA GOVT: TO HOLD 4 ISLAMIC BOND AUCTIONS BY YEAR-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government is targeting to raise IDR1.5 trillion next week in the first of four Islamic bond auctions it plans to hold before the year-end. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA: BUDGET DEFICIT IDR33.23 TRILLION AT END OF SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's budget deficit as of Sept. 30 was IDR33.23 trillion, far below its full-year target of IDR129.8 trillion, the Director General for treasury, Heri Purnomo, told reporters Tuesday. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: BOK TO STAND PAT ON POLICY RATE FOR 8TH STRAIGHT MO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea is likely to leave its base rate at an all-time low of 2.00% in October to ensure ample liquidity for corporates and help sustain a nascent recovery in Asia's fourth-largest economy, economists said. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: MALAYSIA AUG EXPORT DECLINE LIKELY MODERATED VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's exports likely continued falling in August, but at a slower pace than in July, helped by a rise in demand for electronics following improving economic conditions globally, said economists. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: GRAINCORP TO BUY UNITED MALT HLDGS FOR A$757M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian agribusiness \f28 \uc2 \f2 GrainCorp Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Tuesday said it will buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Malt Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the world's fourth largest commercial malt producer, for A$757 million. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BRAMBLES REPLACES CEO AS CHEP US REVIEW ADDS COSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global logistics firm Brambles Ltd. said Tuesday its chief executive will be replaced after the firm flagged an additional US$260 million in costs to improve the quality of its U.S. CHEP pallet business following an eight-month review of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SAMSUNG SEES HIGHER 3Q SALES, OPER PFT; SHARES MUTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's biggest memory chipmaker by revenue, said Tuesday it expects third-quarter sales to rise 19% from a year earlier and median operating profit to come in at KRW4.1 trillion . (published 0135 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:AEON STILL DEEP IN 1H NET LOSS ON CONSUMER ECON FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese retailer Aeon Co. said Tuesday it remained in a net loss in the first half ended Aug. 31, weighed down by consumer belt-tightening amid concerns about the economy, as well as by a special loss at its consumer credit service unit. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POWERLONG CUTS HK IPO TO US$353M FROM US$628M; DELAYS LISTING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Powerlong Real Estate Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it has cut the size of its initial public offering to US$353 million from US$628 million because of volatility in the Hong Kong capital market for new listings and undersubscription of the retail tranche. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JINRO TO RAISE KRW590.4B IN SEOUL IPO AT KRW41,000/SHR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean spirit maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jinro Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it wants to raise KRW590.4 billion from its planned initial public offering on the Korea Exchange later this month. (published 0055 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIRST GEN PLANS PHP15B RIGHTS OFFER; TO HIKE CAPITAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 First Gen Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., one of the Philippines' largest power generation groups, said Tuesday it will increase its authorized capital in line with the company's stock rights offer that will raise around PHP15 billion ($321.2 million). (published 0111 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: LION GROUP RIVAL BID VALUES POLARIS AT A$105.5M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lion-Asia Resources Pte. Ltd. Tuesday launched a cash offer for iron ore junior \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polaris Metals NL\f28 \uc2 \f2  valuing its target at A$105.5 million and trumping an existing share offer from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mineral Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GARTNER SEES NARROWER '09 CHIP REV FALL BUT CUTS '10 FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gartner Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has forecast a narrower 17% fall in worldwide semiconductor revenue this year compared with its previous forecast of a 22.4% drop, because stimulus packages from governments around the world have boosted demand, Bryan Lewis, Gartner research vice president, said Tuesday. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AKAI'S LIQUIDATOR REACHES SETTLEMENT WITH GRANDE HOLDINGS, HO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The liquidator of bankrupt Akai Holdings Ltd. said Tuesday it reached a settlement with Hong Kong-listed Grande Holdings Ltd. and its chairman Christopher Ho in the lawsuit over the collapse of Akai. (published 0204 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: ANZ BK MAY TAKE ANOTHER LOOK AT RBS' CHINA OPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . may take another look at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Scotland Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's banking assets in China after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  pulled out of talks to buy the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a spokesman for the Melbourne-based bank said Tuesday. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA EXPECTS TO RAISE IDR1.8T IN INTERIM DIV FROM 4 COS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government expects to raise up to IDR1.8 trillion in the fourth quarter of 2009 in interim dividend from four state-owned companies, a senior official at the state enterprise ministry said Tuesday. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LARSEN & TOUBRO\f28 \uc2 \f2  GETS FOUR ORDERS WORTH TOTAL OF INR15.13 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Larsen & Toubro Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it has received four orders with a total value of INR15.13 billion. (published 0601 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY UP; JAPAN STKS HIT BY STRONG YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian equity markets mostly advanced Tuesday inspired by solid gains for U.S. stocks, though some markets had slipped off earlier highs or were trading lower. In Tokyo the Nikkei 225 Stock Average had turned negative, as continued strength of the Japanese yen fueled earnings concerns for the country's exporters. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =CHINA ENERGY WATCH: WINDOW OPENS FOR AFRICAN COAL IMPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's search for thermal coal to feed its growing army of power plants has recently taken it to Africa but the trade may last only as long as demand from the continent's usual buyers remains weak. (published 0615 GMT) [ 06-10-09 0707GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091006e5a60009z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
