\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won at 6-mth high on firm stocks, US data\b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2009\par 02:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won hits strongest in over 6-mth on stocks, U.S. job data\par \par \uc2 * Cuts gains on caution over dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Seen rising further on appetite for S.Korean assets (Updates to domestic close)\par \par \uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, May 11 (Reuters) - The South Korean won hit its strongest in more than six months on Monday as foreign investors kept buying Seoul stocks after better-than-expected U.S. job data that bolstered appetite for riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=>, however, gave up some of its early gains as investors became more cautious over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to prevent the country's exporters from losing overseas price competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to rise further as more investors sought assets amid hopes for economic recovery, although the pace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was expected to slow on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities.\par \par \uc2 "Considering firmer stocks and recovery hopes, there are no bearish factors for the won. But I wonder how fast it will rise from this level," said Jeong My-young, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Samsung Futures Inc.\par \par \uc2 "We also need to keep an eye on the authorities, as their actions would just slow the speed of its rise," she added.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean unit was quoted at 1,237.7/8.0 per dollar as of 0600 GMT, compared with Friday's domestic close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,247.0.\par \par \uc2 It strengthened to as much as 1,230.8, the strongest since Oct. 31, 2008.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors bought a net 273.8 billion won worth of stocks on the country's main exchange, helping Seoul shares <.KS11> end up 0.21 percent, recovering earlier losses.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners purchased a combined net 2.12 trillion won in shares during the previous six consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2 Their continuous purchases were expected to support the won, but the further the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose the more wary of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors would grow, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 That, along with demand from exporters, was likely to lock the won in a range, they added.\par \par \uc2 "The won may see some consolidative action within the 1,230-1,246 band for now. Sentiment is turning cautious. There was talk of suspected smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by South Korean authorities as well. There were signs of speculative short covering and good importer demand near 1,230," said Daniel Soh, a strategist at FORECAST Pte Ltd.\par \par \uc2 Investors will be keeping an eye on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy meeting on Tuesday. The Bank of Korea is expected to hold interest rates at a record low of 2.00 percent for the thir month in a row. [ID:nSEO274360]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0600 GMT      0250 GMT    prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           1,237.7/8.0   1,236.9/7.6       1,247.0\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    12.5731/87    12.5765/62    12.5556/47\par  KOSPI <.KS11>           1,415.16      1,414.65      1,412.13\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by )\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090514e55b0001f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
