\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea warns against  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  speculators-Yonhap\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik   \par \uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2009\par 13:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with finance minister)\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 22 (Reuters) - South Korea on Sunday issued a warning against speculative traders as its won \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tumbled on worries about its ability to secure dollars to pay back maturing foreign debt, Yonhap news agency reported.\par \par \uc2 "The government will not sit idle when the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is excessively tilted toward one direction or when there are speculative forces," Yonhap quoted Finance Minister Yoon Jeung-hyun as saying in Phuket, Thailand.\par \par \uc2 Yoon was visiting the Thai resort island to co-chair a meeting of finance ministers from 13 east Asian countries -- 10 southeast Asian countries and China, Japan and South Korea.\par \par \uc2 Finance ministry officials in Seoul could not immediately be reached for comment on the strongest indication of a possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at defending its ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Yoon took office early this month.\par \par \uc2 There has been no report of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by South Korean authorities as the won fell for nine consecutive sessions to trade near an 11-year low against the dollar set in November last year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a statement on Thursday, in which the Bank of Korea dismissed worries about the country's foreign debt burden as overblown, saying the maturing debt was small compared with the country's massive foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said $24.5 billion worth of foreign debt South Korean banks have to pay back or roll over this year was small in value, but warned unstable global markets could make it difficult for South Korean banks to raise sufficient dollars.\par \par \uc2 Yoon's reported comment came hours after Yonhap quoted unnamed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry officials as saying they may use some of the foreign reserves to shore up the tumbling won even if the reserves fall below $200 billion.\par \par \uc2 "Whether the foreign reserves fall below $200 billion is not the subject of consideration at all in deciding whether to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Yonhap quoted an unnamed Bank of Korea official as saying.\par \par \uc2 There has been a perception among traders and analysts that \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  was holding off from dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks because it did not want foreign reserves to fall below $200 billion.\par \par \uc2 South Korean foreign reserves fell to a near four-year low of $200.5 billion at the end of last November as a result of dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for months, before edging up to $201.7 billion by the end of January.\par \par \uc2 Yonhap said another unnamed official at the Ministry of Strategy and Finance also dismissed market talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep foreign reserves above $200 billion.\par \par \uc2 "All of the foreign reserves can be used when it's deemed necessary," the finance ministry official was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea usually carries out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but the finance ministry has the final say.\par \par \uc2 The won has lost 17 percent so far this year to a three-month closing low of 1,506 per dollar on Friday, making it the worst performer among major Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, raising concerns about the country's financial stability as a whole. (Editing by Erica Billingham)\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL-KOREA/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090222e52m0008e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
