\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won hits 2-mth closing low on econ woes\b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2009\par 01:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won at 2-mth closing low on econ worries\par \par \uc2 * Seen falling further on risk aversion\par \par \uc2 * Bank of Korea's rate cut ignored (Updates to domestic close)\par \par \uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 12 (Reuters) - The South Korean won fell against the dollar to hit a two-month closing low on Thursday despite a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cut as worries about a slowing economy and disappointment over a U.S. bank rescue plan hit Seoul shares.\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=>, however, found some relief from persistent caution over possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to weaken further as investors look for safer assets on fears that global stimulus packages will not prove enough to revive the economy, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Technically, the won is more likely to fall more as it broke through the long-time support line of 1,400 (per dollar)," said Jeong My-young, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Samsung Futures Inc.\par \par \uc2 "Risk aversion will strengthen on higher external risks and as South Korean authorities have admitted how serious the state of the economy is," Jeong said.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 1,403.9/4.6 versus the U.S. unit as of 0600 GMT, compared with Wedensday's domestic close of 1,393.5. Thursday's closing was the weakest since Dec. 9, 2008.\par \par \uc2 Investors showed a muted reaction to the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to cut its key policy interest rate by 50 basis points to a record low of 2.00 percent as it was widely expected. [ID:nSP415677]\par \par \uc2 After the rate cut, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said it was uncertain when the economy would bottom out and noted concerns over credit risk persisted in financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Seoul shares <.KS11> ended down 0.87 percent as foreign investors sold a net 202.4 billion won worth of stocks in the country's main exchange.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners unloaded a combined net 319.2 billion won during the previous two consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2 Investors have been disappointed by a $2 trillion rescue programme for U.S. banks unveiled on Tuesday that was seen lacking details and clarity, especially over how a public-private partnership would buy up bad assets.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0345 GMT     0011 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           1,395.8/7.2  1,393.4/4.5      1,393.5\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    15.5089/62   15.4403/09   15.4738/31\par  KOSPI <.KS11>           1,165.55     1,179.42     1,190.18\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Cheon Jong-woo; Editing by Jonathan Hopfner)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090215e52c0000f\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (South Korea near10 interven*)